{"hypothesis_id": "HM7", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-05-17T22:10:00Z", "statement": "FEATURE INVENTORY & ANTI-REDUNDANCY CANON (user 2026-05-17: next agent re-proposes liquidations / ETH-following without knowing they are already in the XGB feature set / or are present-but-DEAD). MANDATORY READ before proposing any feature/data hypothesis. The exact XGB model input for baseline_ref (HM6) and EVERY screen (HA1/HA5/HR1/HA2/H3/baseline_360) = features_v1 (decoded cols 0-55 + CRYPTOLAKE_EXT 56-58; full map in research/CRYPTOLAKE_SCHEMA.md) PLUS per-run live _cond_feats COND_KEYS = {liq_sq_30s,liq_n_30s,liq_sq_120s,liq_n_120s} (signed liquidation qty+counts 30/120s causal, from raw/liquidations; src scripts/ha5_screen.py). Source of truth: src/features.py::FEATURE_KEYS, rust_ingest/src/features.rs, ha5_screen._cond_feats/COND_KEYS, CRYPTOLAKE_SCHEMA.md decoded+DEAD section. ALREADY-COVERED (do NOT re-propose as novel; cite this): (1) LIQUIDATIONS — present & LIVE: features_v1 col19 liquidation_proximity is DEAD/constant(=0.015) BUT EXT cols 56-58 (liq/OI magnitude) are live AND liq_sq/liq_n 30/120s appended live every run incl. HM6 baseline_ref; dedicated test HA5 REFUTED (its note: hand-built liq/OI/funding conditioners 'largely DUPLICATED already-live features_v1 cols'). Only a materially different construction (e.g. cascade-timing, cross-symbol liq contagion) is new. (2) ETH-FOLLOWING / cross-asset — TWO-SIDED: features_v1 ETH cols {14 eth_momentum_1s,15 eth_ofi,16 eth_leading_signal,54 eth_momentum_60s,55 eth_btc_corr_30s} EXIST but are 100% DEAD(zero) in all builds -> via features_v1 NOT a valid test; HOWEVER live cross-asset WAS properly tested: H3 (BTC-lead, btc_cols_live=1.0 -> WEAK symbol-inconsistent marginal, 4/8 cells neg, stacking-only) and HA2 +xasset (8 live BTC-lead+8 live ETH-lead two-head -> REFUTED as posed; SOL-only faint sub-cost whisper d+0.009..0.016, LINK ~0). So ETH/BTC-lead is tested-and-weak, NOT untested; re-proposing naive 'use eth_ cols' is invalid (dead) AND re-proposing 'follow ETH/BTC' duplicates H3/HA2. (3) OI/funding (cols 13,17,44,56-57) — in HA5 (refuted). KEY HONESTY RULE: 'present in features_v1' != 'tested' when the col is in the DEAD list; conversely cross-asset/liq ARE tested via H3/HA2/HA5. A new feature/data hypothesis is admissible ONLY if it is materially different from these and states why, vs this inventory.", "status": "confirmed", "priority_rank": 0, "result_experiment_id": null, "note": "Intercepts the next agent's redundant proposals at the ledger (where hypotheses are proposed). Honest both ways: stops re-proposing already-live/already-refuted signals AND stops mistaking DEAD features_v1 cols for prior tests. Pointers to all source-of-truth files; defers to CRYPTOLAKE_SCHEMA.md for the full decoded map."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HDATA", "note": "Created per user 2026-05-23 as ONE broad, deliberately unbounded training-data axis -- no hardcoded limiters. Dimensions/levels are filled empirically by each run's own pre-registration; this entry imposes none. Provenance is the only constraint.", "priority_rank": 1, "result_experiment_id": null, "rev": 1, "statement": "OPEN data-axis container (exploratory conditional-optimization, HD1-style; deliberately UNBOUNDED). QUESTION: under what training-data composition do models best extract directional signal? DELIVERABLE = an accumulating conditional rank_IC surface over training-data-composition variables, filled cell-by-cell over time. NO dimension or level is pre-enumerated or bounded by THIS entry: any aspect of the training data -- what data, from where, over what span and prediction horizon, in what single-/multi-/cross-asset structure, read by any probe model -- is in scope; what varies and at what levels is declared by each run's own frozen pre-registration, never constrained here. Rigor lives ONLY in per-result provenance (data_source, n_eff, split_method, cost basis, repro_cmd) so the surface stays trustworthy and reusable -- not in restricting axes. SELECTION during search = robust marginal delta_ic vs a declared baseline_ref (standing SELECTION POLICY); the section-5 economic gate is a DEMOTED secondary annotation, never the headline or a per-cell kill. Subsumes the scattered open data notes (HD1 multi-symbol/horizon pooling 'real n_eff multiplier', data-scale) into one container instead of fragmenting into correlated narrow overlapping hypotheses.", "status": "active", "ts": "2026-05-22T23:08:46Z"}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD2", "note": "rev28 - sub-60s substrate built + economic surface characterized (levers #4,#2 done). Binding lever = vol-model precision, not the direction wall. Headline = the surface + universal argmax (tp0.30/sl0.05/45-60s) + the lever that drives alpha; the maker break-even read is a secondary deploy annotation, not the framing. Scripts: scripts/subs60_orch.py (build), subs60_within.py (two-axis predictivity), subs60_gridsim2.py (oracle/deployable grid), subs60_finepath.py (100ms fine path + continuous conviction). Recovery doc: mamba2plan.md (gitignored). Uncommitted append. git 3099e7d.", "priority_rank": 1, "result_experiment_id": "subs60-20260528_gridsim_deployable", "rev": 28, "statement": "HD2 rev28 - SUB-60s SUBSTRATE + ECONOMIC ALPHA SURFACE (exploratory characterization; levers #4 fine-path and #2 selectivity executed, #1 vol-head precision and #3 two-head Mamba-2 staged). HEADLINE SURFACE (8 Binance USDT-perps, 60s hold, grid_sim TP/SL, Binance-standard fees): the deployable EV/trade surface is governed by ONE argmax region and ONE binding lever. ARGMAX config is universal across all 8 symbols: tp0.30 / sl0.05 (reward:risk 6:1) / hold 45-60s / fill-latency 150ms. TWO-AXIS PREDICTIVITY: vol-head ranks |move|>=13bp at AUC 0.78-0.89 but rare-event PRECISION only 21-40%; dir-head reaches accuracy 0.55-0.65 on the selective conviction tail (direction is NOT a hard coin-flip wall - it sits +5..+15pp above base on the tail). ECONOMIC SURFACE by gate/path/tier: (a) ORACLE ceiling (perfect vol-head, realized-|rH60|>=13bp gate): VIP0/zero-fee +5.4..+7.2 bp/trade, maker +0.7..+1.7 bp; (b) DEPLOYABLE (vol-MODEL gate, no look-ahead): VIP0 +0.9..+2.0 bp, maker -4.1..-5.0 bp; (c) FINE 100ms forward path recovers ~1.5x gross vs the 1s coarse grid (the 1s grid undercounts intra-second TP touches ~30-45%); (d) SELECTIVE top-0.2% (~30 trades/day, combined vol x dir conviction percentile): VIP0 +1.0..+3.6 bp, maker still -2..-6 bp. BINDING LEVER (what drives alpha, NOT a kill-verdict): the oracle-vs-deployable gap is almost entirely vol-MODEL PRECISION - the realized-vol gate clears the maker floor, the model gate does not; direction holds on the tail and selectivity+fine-path each add gross but neither closes the maker gap alone. => the highest-marginal-alpha next axis is vol-head precision (multi-minute realized-vol + funding/OI trend + basis + time-of-day over a longer pre-window), then the two-head Mamba-2. Net-positive today only at VIP0/zero-fee (fund-pitch upper bound). PIPELINE FIX (this rev): the Rust feature_builder readers were rebuilt for the FLAT raw schema (bid_0_price..ask_19_size, ts NANOSECONDS->ms; trades flat amount+side[dict-cast Utf8]; funding rate fallback) - the prior readers expected a nested FSL schema absent from the bucket. Added liquidations (cols 56-58: signed liq 5s/30s + log1p liq_intensity 60s), open-interest (cols 59-60: oi_delta 30s/300s), full OBI ladder (col 61=OBI_L20, 62=OBI_L1 top-of-book, 63=OBI_L10); ETH cols 14/16/54 repurposed to clean eth_logret last-price-at lags {1,2,5}s; NUM_FEATURES 56->64. SUBSTRATE: feats_sub60/ on GCS = 2776 sym-days, 8 symbols (BTC/ETH/BNB/SOL/XRP/DOGE/LINK/LTC), 2025-05-09..2026-05-08, dense 1s decision grid, 64-col X, labels rH_{15,30,45,60} in bp. METHOD (per CLAUDE.md + user constraint 'no discrete pass/fail gates at this phase'): characterize the CONTINUOUS alpha surface - ridge-predict |move| ranked continuously, EV-vs-conviction decile curve, selective-tail percentiles; logreg fit_cap=25000 subsample (slow VM BLAS); overlap-aware throughput (per-trade EV unaffected, only trades/day inflates). DATA CONTRACT: GCP project-0998ac51-36ba-445c-bc7, bucket gs://market-data-0998ac51, feats_sub60/SYM/YYYY-MM-DD.npz; raw/{book,trades,funding,liquidations,open_interest}/exchange=BINANCE_FUTURES. Fees = Binance standard CONSTANT (maker 0.04/0.07, taker 0.10/0.10 round-trip); VIP0 zero-fee = fund-pitch upper bound only. STAGED NEXT: #1 vol-head precision (raise gross above the maker floor); #3 two-head Mamba-2 (rev27 frozen spec: head A FL/NONFL gate BCE-all, head B UP/DN BCE-directional-only) on feats_sub60 stream-2 + raw LOB stream-1, Modal GPU. rev27's two-head training was NOT executed in rev28 (substrate build + economic characterization only). rev1-27 UNCHANGED.", "status": "testing", "ts": "2026-05-28T00:00:00Z"}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD2", "note": "rev29 = frozen pre-reg for lever #1 (vol-head precision), the binding lever from rev28. PRE-RUN: nothing built. Requires VM feature-rebuild (cost gate) -> needs user sign-off before running, per CLAUDE.md. RL side-experiment (2026-05-28) corroborated direction adds ~nothing even frictionless (logits contribution -55pp heldout) -> precision of the VOL gate, not more direction modeling, is the right next axis. Uncommitted append. git 3099e7d.", "priority_rank": 1, "result_experiment_id": null, "rev": 29, "statement": "HD2 rev29 - LEVER #1 VOL-HEAD PRECISION (pre-registered, frozen PRE-RUN; awaiting VM-rebuild cost sign-off). CONTEXT (rev28 surface): the deployable-vs-oracle maker gap is the BINDING lever and it is almost entirely vol-MODEL PRECISION - the oracle (realized |rH60|>=13bp gate) clears maker at +0.7..+1.7 bp/trade, the deployable vol-MODEL gate sits at -4.1..-5.0 bp because its rare-event precision is only 21-40% (AUC 0.78-0.89 ranks but does not separate at the 13bp floor); direction is NOT the wall (dir_acc 0.55-0.65 on the tail), and #4 fine-path (~1.5x gross) + #2 selectivity (top-0.2%) each add gross but neither closes the maker gap. QUESTION: does enriching the vol-head with LONGER-HORIZON + FUNDAMENTAL predictors raise gate precision enough to move deployable-maker EV/trade materially toward break-even at matched trades/day? FROZEN PREDICTOR SET (added to feats_sub60, computed over a longer PRE-window from raw): (a) multi-minute trailing realized vol {1,5,15,30 min}; (b) funding-rate level + trend; (c) open-interest level + delta {1,5,30 min}; (d) basis (perp mark vs index/spot) if present in raw, else omit and note; (e) time-of-day / session encoding (vol seasonality). MODEL: retrain the vol head P(|rH60|>=13bp) (logreg baseline + small GBM as the nonlinearity arm, since 'code complexity is our edge') on the day-based 65/35 honest split with 60s embargo. PRIMARY DELIVERABLE (continuous surface, NO pass/fail gate per CLAUDE.md + user constraint): (i) the vol-head precision-recall / precision-vs-coverage curve vs the current 64-col baseline, and (ii) the DEPLOYABLE-maker EV-per-trade-vs-gate-precision surface from a re-run grid_sim (same universal argmax tp0.30/sl0.05, hold 45-60s, fill-latency 150ms) at matched trades/day. The lever's magnitude = how far the deployable-maker EV moves toward 0 as precision rises, and whether it crosses break-even at a deployable coverage (>=10 trades/day across 8 syms). SECONDARY (demoted deploy annotation, NOT selection): absolute maker break-even y/n. COST GATE: the new predictors require a VM feature-rebuild over a longer pre-window from raw/{book,trades,funding,open_interest} (egress/compute) - scope + user sign-off REQUIRED before building; rev29 is the spec only, nothing built/run. DATA CONTRACT: GCP project-0998ac51, gs://market-data-0998ac51, extend feats_sub60/SYM/DATE.npz with the new columns; fees Binance-standard constant (maker 0.04/0.07). STAGED AFTER: #3 two-head Mamba-2 (rev27 spec) on the enriched stream-2 + raw LOB stream-1. rev1-28 UNCHANGED.", "status": "testing", "ts": "2026-05-28T01:00:00Z"}
