 8.4 bp (n=20, sign/median confirmed, magnitude noisy). LEVER surfaced this rev (user insight) = the '5% most-volatile deviation' hardcoded into Model A is PERIOD-DEPENDENT; a rolling/regime-adaptive threshold is the right form, for walk-forward folds AND live. SECONDARY deploy-gate annotation only: the maker-SIM net OOS clears the 4bp maker floor robustly, but fills are SIMULATED (touch/queue/MISS) -- live-execution confirmation (paper trading DOGE) is the next test, not a deploy verdict. UNTESTED: live execution; more symbols; shorter trailing-window threshold; per-fold HP re-tune. rev1 UNCHANGED.", "status": "testing", "ts": "2026-06-03T21:35:00Z"}
{"compute_cost_usd": "~$2 (GCE n2-standard-8 in-region; multi-hold label build ~23min + several walk-forward sweeps ~25-50min each, all on cached data)", "compute_time": "label build ~23min; horizon/noA/baseline/vol-norm walk-forwards ~25-50min each (B-full on full universe is the bottleneck)", "expected_lift": "regime-robust zero-fee surface (Sharpe vs horizon x policy x vol-norm), not a single number", "hypothesis_id": "HD3", "note": "Zero-fee (USDC maker) pivot of HD3. Per-fold preds cached (wf_cache/DOGE_h{15,30,60}s) -> deploy/metric sweeps now instant. Demo trading keys verified (Binance Futures testnet). git 436503a.", "prerequisites": "multi-hold maker labels (subs60_makerlabel_build --holds-sec) + husdc maker-sim binaries on VM + per-fold preds caches", "priority_rank": 1, "result_experiment_id": "xgb-20260604_doge_zerofee_volnorm_baseline", "rev": 3, "statement": "HD3 rev3 (EXPLORATORY -> ZERO-fee sub-minute directional-maker surface). PIVOT: trade USDC (maker fee 0; net=gross) and sub-minute holds. QUESTIONS answered this rev: (1) HORIZON 15/30/60s -- 30s is the risk-adjusted argmax; 15s collapses CAUSALLY (Sharpe~0; the post-hoc 15s edge was look-ahead); Model-A vol-AUC ~0.84-0.85 flat across horizons. (2) DO WE NEED the vol-gate A? At matched CAUSAL frequency noA (B-full direction, no gate) >= AxB and is the deploy argmax (the vol-gate's threshold drift hurts the product). (3) SELECTION must be CAUSAL not post-hoc: post-hoc top-N is look-ahead and inflates ~3-4x; the deployable rolling/frozen threshold is what counts; a learned trade-EV selectivity model underperformed the pA*pB heuristic (per-trade EV too noisy to regress; the A(vol)xB(dir) decomposition is better-conditioned). (4) The per-fold edge concentrated in fold-2 -- DIAGNOSED as a VOLATILITY COVARIATE SHIFT: DOGE vol declined monotonically over the year so the trailing-200d TRAIN is always more volatile than the recent TEST, EXCEPT f2 whose Jan-Feb spike matches train (test/train p95|rH30|: 0.67/0.73/1.01/0.91/0.64/0.85); microstructure feats scale with vol -> compress in calm regimes -> model (A AND B) under-captures. FIX = causal trailing per-feature z-score -> vol-invariant feats. BASELINE (vol-norm noA 30s causal target-5/day, actual 1.7/day, ZERO fee): annualized Sharpe +2.42, EV +4.26 bp/trade, hit 51.1%, +7.14 bp/day, BROAD per-fold [3.1,4.5,1.9,-1.1,4.0,-1.0] (f2 +23.2->+1.9, calm f0 -0.3->+3.1). The non-normalized annS +5.39 was f2-spike-inflated (regime-dependent); the broad +2.42 is the honest regime-robust baseline. METRIC NOTE: AUC/dir-acc is SIZE-BLIND; size-weighted EV/Sharpe is the right lens (hit ~51% yet +EV because wins are bigger -- momentum on big moves). SECONDARY (deploy annotation): maker-SIM fills, not live; one symbol/year; HP frozen (non-norm-tuned); zero-fee assumes USDC maker 0% (venue-confirm). This is the conditional surface + the regime-robustness fix, NOT a deploy verdict. NEXT: HP re-tune (Optuna, per-fold) on normalized feats; targeted vol-norm; more symbols; live paper trading (testnet ready). rev1-2 UNCHANGED.", "status": "testing", "ts": "2026-06-04T13:10:00Z"}
{"compute_cost_usd": "~$1 (GCE n2-standard-8 in-region; per-fold Optuna A+B 25 trials each, ~40-55min on cached vol-normed feats)", "compute_time": "per-fold Optuna (A on AUC + B on IC, 25 trials, TUNE_SUB=200k) ~40-55min", "expected_lift": "size-aware-tuned regime-robust zero-fee surface (annS vs policy x budget) + the B IC(val) signal-thickness map", "hypothesis_id": "HD3", "note": "Iterates rev3 vol-norm baseline. Size-aware B-tuning (IC) restores deploy to frozen parity after the AUC-Optuna run broke it; confirms the tuning metric (not HP/norm) was the lever, and the signal-thickness ceiling. git 0a4f205.", "prerequisites": "maker_labels_h/DOGE.npz (multi-hold) + husdc maker-sim feats + optuna on VM", "priority_rank": 1, "result_experiment_id": "xgb-20260606_doge_zerofee_ic_tuned_baseline", "rev": 4, "statement": "HD3 rev4 (EXPLORATORY -> size-aware B-tuning of the zero-fee sub-minute directional-maker surface). QUESTION answered this rev: is XGBoost-B's hyperparameter / tuning-metric a lever for the thin direction signal? SURFACE: B's size-aware signal IC=corr(pB-0.5, netl-nets) on sub-val is STABLE and positive on all 6 folds [+0.0143,+0.0206,+0.0178,+0.0109,+0.0267,+0.0236] (mean ~+0.019, no sign flip) -- B predicts the better maker SIDE of LARGE moves above chance on every fold; the AUC~0.52 was size-blind and hid it. ARGMAX (policy x budget) = noA (B-full direction, no vol-gate) target-10/day: annualized Sharpe +2.45, EV +1.40 bp/trade, hit 53.0%, +13.83 bp/day, per-fold(%) [12.1,9.8,-3.1,1.9,7.4,-5.9] (4/6 positive, f2 neutralized to -3.1). noA t5 = annS +2.18 / EV +1.76 bp / hit 55.7% / per-fold [6.7,5.6,-0.9,2.4,4.7,-5.2] (HIGHER EV/trade, cleaner). noA dominates AxB at both budgets (AxB t5 +0.15, t10 -2.11; the vol-gate sheds alpha in zero-fee MM). METRIC-LEVER FINDING: three independent ways of turning the B knob around the SAME single signal converge to annS ~+2.4 -- frozen HP +2.42, Optuna-on-AUC +0.30 (broke the deploy: size-blind metric + val-overfit on a ~0.52 coin-flip), Optuna-on-IC +2.45 (restores frozen parity). So the lever was the TUNING METRIC, not HP/norm-scheme; size-aware (IC) tuning is the correct knob but does NOT lift the CEILING, which is set by the THICKNESS of the single direction signal (IC~0.019). HP/objective/normalization cannot thicken it -- raising the ceiling needs more symbols (portfolio Sharpe) or a new uncorrelated signal. DECLARED working BASELINE = noA t10 IC-tuned, annS +2.45 (supersedes rev3 frozen-HP +2.42). SECONDARY (deploy annotation): maker-SIM fills not live; one symbol/year; zero-fee assumes USDC maker 0% (venue-confirm; testnet ready, DOGEUSDT, 5000 USDT demo); annS scales with sqrt(trd/day) so t10>t5 is partly frequency (EV/trade higher at t5). NEXT: more symbols (portfolio Sharpe on the same 30s zero-fee noA), then a new uncorrelated signal. rev1-3 UNCHANGED.", "status": "testing", "ts": "2026-06-06T16:10:00Z"}
{"compute_cost_usd": "~$3 (GCE n2-standard-8 in-region; 3x relabel ~20-30min each (3 parallel) + 3x per-fold A+B Optuna deploy ~30-50min)", "compute_time": "relabel pegged-exit+qm1 ~20-30min/symbol (3 parallel); AxB+noA deploy (A-AUC + B-IC Optuna, 6 folds) ~30-50min/symbol", "expected_lift": "conditional surface: AxB/noA EV & annS as a function of (entry-queue-position x policy x symbol x budget) under maker-only pegged exit", "hypothesis_id": "HD3", "note": "Two-leg realism (pegged maker-only exit + always-last entry). Key informative result: the noA-vs-AxB ranking flips with the entry-fill assumption (qm0 front -> noA wins; qm1 last -> AxB wins) -- recorded as a measured conditional, not a universal claim. grid_sim_exitdbg.rs mirrored to scripts/. git af2ed18.", "prerequisites": "grid_sim_exitdbg built on VM (/tmp/edbg_target) + maker_labels_pegexit_qm1 labels + optuna on VM", "priority_rank": 1, "result_experiment_id": "xgb-20260606_pegexit_alwayslast_axb_noA_doge_eth_btc", "rev": 5, "statement": "HD3 rev5 (EXPLORATORY -> realistic maker EXIT + SYMMETRIC always-last fills; conditional surface). This rev makes BOTH legs realistic and measures how the noA-vs-AxB ranking depends on the fill assumptions. (1) The OLD exit (hold-to-timeout, 2s maker-at-mid else taker-cross, commissions 0) was probed: 59-83% of BTC/ETH exits were TAKER charged 0 fee; at a 5bp taker fee that exit alone ~10x the per-trade EV -> motivated a maker-only exit. (2) Built a PEGGED maker-only exit (simulate_pegged_exit: close-limit pegged to touch, ALWAYS LAST, re-quote on adverse move, held-until-filled, mark@last-touch, no taker). (3) Set ENTRY symmetric ALWAYS-LAST (queue_mult=1). CONDITIONAL SURFACE (DOGE/ETH/BTC, 2025-05-09..2026-05-08, 30s, zero maker fee + no taker, BOTH legs always-last): AxB-t5 = DOGE EV+4.17/annS+3.40, ETH +3.50/+3.24 (5-6/6 folds pos), BTC -0.14 (~flat); noA = negative for all three (t5 annS DOGE-5.81/ETH-21.5/BTC-28.8). QUALIFIED: the noA<->AxB ranking is CONDITIONAL ON ENTRY-FILL REALISM, measured: front-of-queue(qm0) entry -> noA positive & dominant; always-last(qm1) entry -> noA negative, AxB dominant (DOGE entry-isolation, old exit: qm0 EV+1.40 -> qm1 -1.18; entry fill 0.978->0.82). So 'is vol-gate A needed' answers CONDITIONALLY: no under front-of-queue, yes under always-last -- for THESE symbols/year/horizon/execution ONLY; re-measure for any other market/model/window/execution. Entry fill rate always-last: DOGE~0.86, ETH~0.78, BTC~0.55 (deep book -> miss more -> BTC marginal). Direction signal IC stable (DOGE~0.04/BTC~0.056/ETH~0.066). ALL prior project results (+5.73, baselines, portfolio, rev3-4) were under qm0 FRONT-OF-QUEUE entry -> conditioned on that optimistic entry. CAVEATS: maker-sim fills, entry_q queue proxy, no re-quote latency, favorable-side queue-priority kept (mild), one symbol-set/year, per-trade annS overstates vs daily ~1.3-1.5x. REPRODUCIBLE: subs60_makerlabel_build (--grid-bin grid_sim_exitdbg --exit-queue-mult 1 --queue-mults 1.0) + subs60_xgb_optuna_ic {sym} maker_labels_pegexit_qm1 0. rev1-4 UNCHANGED.", "status": "testing", "ts": "2026-06-06T22:40:00Z"}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 6, "ts": "2026-07-05T12:40:00Z", "status": "testing", "statement": "HD3 rev6 (EXPLORATORY -> HONEST TIME-BASED label semantics + live decision cadence; frozen spec pre-registered BEFORE the year build/train). MOTIVATION (2026-07-05 optimism audit of the deployed robust2 weights, by code+data): (a) CL books are event-driven 1.45-2.32 snaps/s, so the tick-count sim windows (entry 120t, hold 282t, chase to path end ~700t) actually priced entry ~51-83s, hold ~2-3 MINUTES and a free mark-at-touch on 51-53pct of exits -- B was trained/backtested on a different horizon than the live 30s executor; (b) live decides every 10.8s wall-clock while data moves tick-by-tick. FIX UNDER TEST: rebuild the full CL year of maker labels with WALL-CLOCK windows -- decisions on a TIME-UNIFORM 3s grid (live cadence semantics, ~28.8k/day vs 8k), entry window 12.8s from decision ts, hold {15,30,60}s FROM THE FILL ts, pegged maker-only exit chase 300s (recorder study: 98.6pct fill in 5min; residual ran-out marked at touch), always-last both legs (qm=1, exit_qm=1), 0 maker fee, robust FB feats at the same ticks, real btc_lead, time-based rH15/30/60; CL trade triplication deduped by id. THEN retrain/test the SAME frozen protocol as robust2: subs60_xgb_optuna_ic (W=200/T=30/EMB=2 walk-forward folds, per-fold Optuna A-AUC + B-IC, causal_rolling day-tau deploy) on maker_labels_tb3s, DOGE, budgets 5/10/20/40; PRIMARY variant trains with btc cols ZEROED (exact live-input parity), secondary with real btc (measures what wiring BTC into live would add). PRIMARY DELIVERABLE (exploratory): the conditional EV surface -- EV/trade + annS + fill-rate as a function of (budget x hold {15/30/60}s x fold), argmax regime + fold-stability, compared cell-by-cell against the tick-based rev5/robust2 surface to quantify how much of the historical edge was horizon/marking optimism vs real 30s signal. SECONDARY (confirmatory, separate question): whether the honest-label model at t10/30s beats the deployed robust2 weights on the recorder-EV protocol -> candidate weight swap for axb-live (user decision). PRE-REGISTERED VERIFICATION ALREADY DONE: rust time-mode replicated in python on 500 samples x2 sides, 0 mismatches; hold wall-clock median 30.76s p90 33.5s; ran-out 0/702 at 300s chase; path span p10 503s >= 343s needed.", "prerequisites": "husdc build_samples+grid_sim_exitdbg rebuilt with time-mode on hd2 (/tmp/husdc_target, src /tmp/husdc_ri, mirrored to scripts/); robust FB /tmp/fb_target; CL raw book+trades 2025-05-09..2026-06-02 in gs://market-data-0998ac51/raw (369+ days); feats_sub60 BTC mids", "expected_lift": "surface: honest-horizon EV by (budget x hold x fold); expectation from the recorder-EV honest rerun is that top-selectivity cells survive (t10 order +5..+15bp gross) while unselected/mid cells shrink vs tick-based labels; genuinely uncertain -- that is the point of the rebuild", "compute_time": "label build ~40s/day x ~369 days on 2 shards ~2-3h (hd2 n2-standard-8); optuna_ic on ~10.5M rows x 7 folds ~6-12h; total <1 day, ~USD 5-10 VM time", "note": "Build script scripts/subs60_build_tb3s_labels.py -> research_runs/maker_labels_tb3s/{daily/,DOGE.npz}. Frozen BEFORE launch; any deviation gets a new rev. Live executor semantics this mirrors: GTX entry at touch 12.8s window, hold 30s from fill, maker-only pegged exit chase (never-taker), decisions on wall clock.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 6, "ts": "2026-07-05T18:05:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "tb3s-20260705_honest_timebased_decomposition", "statement": "HD3 rev6 RESULT (forensic decomposition; all cells measured, pipeline bit-validated). HONEST SURFACE (time-based windows: entry 12.8s from decision, hold 30s FROM FILL, pegged maker chase 300s, 3s time-uniform grid, 386d, 7 folds, live-parity btc=0): AxB EV/tr = t5 -3.77 / t10 -3.20 / t20 -3.30 / t40 -3.16 bp gross; real-btc variant ~+0.3..0.6bp better, sign unchanged; B IC(val) +0.049..+0.090 on all folds (signal alive; selection does not convert it at 30s). ROOT CAUSE OF THE HISTORICAL POSITIVE YEAR (found by cell isolation): makerlabel_build matched each decision point to the NEAREST build sample within +-2.5s -> in ~half the rows the entry was priced/queued at a book tick UP TO 2.5s IN THE PAST relative to feature time (feature window overlaps the trade start) = label-matching lookahead. Isolation cell (robust2 F + robust2 grid + SAME tick windows, labels rebuilt at the EXACT feature tick): +3.77 -> -1.74 t5 (perfold -7.5,+14.9,-7.2,-3.5,+0.1,-11.0), +1.95 -> -0.72 t10. ~5.5bp/tr of the recorded edge was the matching artifact; qm1 baseline (+4.17/annS+3.40, RESEARCH_LOG s19) used the same matching and carries the same inflation. FULL CELL MATRIX (EV/tr t5): qm1 matched +4.17 | robust2 matched +3.77 | robust2 EXACT -1.74 | my-grid exact legacy repro +0.91 | honest 30s 3s-grid -3.77 | LIVE-CONFIG (2-3min-trained B, honest 30s exec, ts-join eval) -2.35 (perfold -2.0,-4.6,-9.3,-2.6,+1.2,+2.7,-0.0 — the two most recent folds positive, consistent with the matching-clean 7d recorder-EV +10.3 = regime wobble, not persistent edge). PIPELINE VALIDATION: feature-swap cell (FB-full recomputed at robust2 ticks + robust2 labels) reproduced the recorded +3.77 BIT-EXACTLY -> new build path exonerated; also proves robust2 F == FB-full (splice equality gate), i.e. qm1-vs-robust2 differ ONLY in vol cols 34-39, which alone re-shuffled the fold structure (9.6,11.3,4.9,2.5,4.0,-0.6 -> -1.1,23.2,16.0,-1.9,-3.4,-3.9). SELECTIVITY MECHANICS (user hypothesis, tested on saved per-fold artifacts, no retrain): take-clustering at 3s grid is real (47-50pct of takes <60s apart) but explains <=1-2.5bp (subsample to 12s/24s: -3.67/-2.40; cooldown 30/60/120s: best -1.11; equal-quantile t20-vs-t5@12s: no artifact) — does not flip the sign. CONDITIONAL SUMMARY: under exact label alignment this model family shows ~0 (+-1.5 fold-noise) EV on the OLD 2-3min semantics and -2.4..-3.8 on honest 30s live semantics, all budgets; the only positive support for live is 7d recorder-EV + the 2 most recent folds (regime-conditional).", "note": "Artifacts: research_runs/maker_labels_tb3s{,_legacy}/(DOGE.npz, OPTUNA_IC_*.json, PERFOLD_*.npz), maker_labels_robust2_fbfull/, maker_labels_robust2_exactlab/. Scripts: subs60_build_tb3s_labels.py (time+legacy modes), tb3s_selectivity/crosscell/featswap2/exactlab (scratchpad->VM /home/delmi). Time-mode rust verified vs python replication 1000 samples 0 mismatch; hold wall-clock median 30.76s. RESEARCH_LOG s20. Live axb-live left RUNNING (user decision pending).", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 6, "ts": "2026-07-05T19:10:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "tb3s-20260705_leak_refuted_structural_variance", "statement": "HD3 rev6 CORRECTION (supersedes the lookahead attribution in the 18:05 rev6 entry; that entry stays per append-only). MODEL-FREE leak test on the +-2.5s label matching REFUTED the lookahead mechanism: build grid is dense (40k/day) so |t_feat - t_build| median ~0.3s, overlap move p90 = 0.91bp; corr(r_overlap, netl_matched) = -0.031 vs exact -0.042 (both ~0/negative); follow-overlap-side tail EV negative on both. Row-level matched-vs-exact across the year: corr 0.99, mean diff -0.001bp (NO systematic shift), fill agreement 97.4pct, yB target agreement 95.0pct. NO leak, NO artifact — the user challenge was correct. REVISED INTERPRETATION of +3.77 -> -1.74: a ~5pct perturbation of B training targets (pure label noise, zero mean shift) swings the year walk-forward total by ~5.5bp => the protocol year-EV estimate has STRUCTURAL VARIANCE of several bp (top-5/day tail selection x deep trees x per-fold Optuna). All old-semantics measurements (+4.17 qm1, +3.77 robust2, +0.91 my-grid, -1.74 exact-labels) are draws from one wide distribution, mean ~+1 +-3 => THE YEAR NEVER STATISTICALLY IDENTIFIED AN EDGE at the old semantics (retroactively explains fold reshuffle from a 6-col feature swap, DOGE-only positivity, robust2 winter concentration). The honest-30s cells are consistently negative across ALL draws (t5/t10/t20/t40, btc 0/real, 30s-trained and 2-3min-trained cross-cell: -3.8..-2.4) => at live 30s semantics the result is stable: adverse floor, no compensating selection. PROCESS RULE derived: before trusting any year-EV from this protocol family, run a PERTURBATION GATE (retrain on label-jittered/target-flipped copies; the spread IS the error bar).", "note": "Model-free scripts tb3s_leakproof.py + row-level comparison (VM /home/delmi). Prior rev6 entry 18:05 lookahead claim WITHDRAWN; RESEARCH_LOG s20a