{"hypothesis_id": "HD4", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-07-12T09:10:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "dir10-20260712_cl_screen_tailamend", "statement": "HD4 rev1 AMENDMENT (user question: reported cuts vs deployed ~0.02% selectivity) - TOP-K-PER-DAY EXTREME-TAIL CUT, same data/metrics, no ML (scripts/subs60_dir10_tail.py; K=5/10/28/280 per day = ~0.017%/0.035%/0.1%/1% of ~28.8k day windows; K=5 mirrors the deployed t5 day budget). FINDING: the model-free capture curve SATURATES into the tail - going 1% -> 0.017% adds only ~10-25%, unlike the trained score where tail selection is everything. @H=10s K=5 (bp per 10s, gross mid move; d+ = frac of days with positive day-mean): BTC imb_L5 +1.02 hit 0.718 d+0.84, OBI_L1 +0.95 hit 0.717; ETH COMP +1.01 hit 0.566, OBI_L1 +0.92 hit 0.63; DOGE OBI_L1 +1.14 hit 0.595; XRP COMP +1.35, OBI_L1 +0.95 (K=5 cells are 5-obs/day noisy; K=28 confirms the level: BTC +0.90, ETH +0.83, DOGE +1.07, XRP +1.03 all d+>=0.82). vs K=280 (1%): BTC +0.84, ETH +0.81, DOGE +0.93, XRP +0.93 - d+ ~1.00 everywhere. CAUTION CELL: f32 top3_asym INVERTS in the extreme tail on thin books (DOGE K=5 @10s -0.83bp, XRP -0.70bp, while its K=280 is positive) - per-signal tail monotonicity must be checked, do not assume; book-shape (OBI_L1/imb_L5) and COMP stay monotone-positive into the tail on all 4 symbols. Implication for hypothesis-2: the extension gate operates conditional on already-selected trades (3-5/day), not at 0.02% unconditional selectivity; the relevant magnitudes are the q90-tail ~+0.6-0.9bp/10s levels, which hold (and slightly grow) into any realistic tail.", "priority_rank": 1, "note": "Artifacts research_runs/h2_dir10/{SYM}_tail.npz; units dir10t-{SYM} on dir10-1 (restart->stop, ~2min/symbol, no raw book - reused h2_dir10 dailies + tb3s F). VM stopped again."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD4", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-07-12T09:40:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "dir10-20260712_cl_chain", "statement": "HD4 rev1 CHAIN AMENDMENT PREREG (user rule, stage-1.5, still model-free): chained 10s holds. Episode = tick with |S| >= theta_entry (per-day quantile of |S| over valid ticks, same-day convention as the screen - NOT causal, noted), direction = sign(S); each step captures that tick's 10s forward mid move (h2_dir10 R[h10], [8,10]s window); at +10s re-evaluate at the nearest 3s-grid tick (tol 2s): CONTINUE while sign(S)==dir AND |S| >= theta_cont, else STOP with reason flip (sign reversed) / weak (same sign below theta_cont) / data (no tick or invalid r10) / cap (30 steps). Episodes NON-OVERLAPPING (greedy forward scan, chain consumes its ticks) -> also quantifies the clustering of the earlier top-K cells. SWEEP: S in {f62 OBI_L1, COMP} x theta_entry {q90,q99} x theta_cont {q50, =entry}; symbols BTC,ETH,DOGE,XRP; CL year. METRICS per cell: episodes/day, mean length, P(len>=2), P(len>=3), bp/episode total vs step-1-only (= the ADDED value of chaining), pooled per-step-position capture k=1..6 (does persistence keep earning?), stop-reason shares, day-level share of positive added-capture. Limits: gross mid moves, no exit-repricing cost; unconditional starts (not fill+150s of real trades); ~<=2s splice noise between step endpoint and next decision tick. Script scripts/subs60_dir10_chain.py; artifacts {SYM}_chain.npz.", "priority_rank": 1, "note": "Runs on dir10-1 from saved artifacts only (no raw book). Cost ~minutes."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD4", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-07-12T10:20:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "dir10-20260712_cl_chain", "statement": "HD4 rev1 CHAIN AMENDMENT MEASURED - the user's chained-10s-hold rule works model-free, and its EFFECTIVE FORM is now known: the continuation threshold must be SOFTER than the entry threshold. SURFACE (CL year, non-overlapping episodes, gross mid bp per episode; cells = sig x q_entry x q_cont): (1) ARGMAX RULE = enter at strong signal (q90/q99), CONTINUE while |S|>q50 same-sign: mean chain length 1.3-1.75 windows, P(len>=2) 0.20-0.42, P(len>=3) 0.05-0.19; chaining ADDS +0.16..+0.28bp per episode on top of the first window's +0.65..+0.97bp (~+20-35%), day-stable: added-capture positive on 95-100% of days at q90 entry (83-97% at q99). BTC/ETH add MORE (+0.20..+0.28) than DOGE/XRP (+0.16..+0.19) - consistent with the rev1 predictivity ordering. (2) STRICT CONTINUATION (q_cont=q_entry) KILLS chaining: length collapses to 1.01-1.11, added +0.00..+0.07bp - the literal 'still strong enough' rule at entry strength almost never fires twice; softening to q50 is what creates 2-4-window chains. (3) PER-STEP conditional capture stays POSITIVE through steps 2-4 everywhere (BTC f62: +0.76/+0.48/+0.44/+0.37; ETH +0.77/+0.52/+0.49/+0.50; DOGE decays fastest +0.88/+0.60/+0.51/+0.28; XRP +0.80/+0.58/+0.53/+0.50) - persistence keeps earning at a decaying but positive rate, so the chain rule harvests real continuation, not noise re-entry. (4) STOP REASONS at qc=q50: ~57-65% sign flip / ~30-43% weak / <=0.22 data - exits are mostly genuine reversals. Episode totals at q99/q50: BTC +1.09, ETH +1.02-1.06, DOGE +1.13, XRP +1.02-1.12 bp per ~13-17s episode. LIMITS unchanged: gross mid moves (no exit-repricing cost), unconditional starts (not fill+150s of real h150 trades), same-day quantile thresholds (non-causal within day). Stage 2 proper = replay on real h150 trades with pegged-exit cost.", "priority_rank": 1, "note": "Artifacts research_ru