{"hypothesis_id": "HD4", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-07-12T10:50:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "dir10-20260712_cl_chain_h3060", "statement": "HD4 rev1 CHAIN HORIZON AMENDMENT PREREG: rerun the chained-hold episode sim with step quantum HOR_S=30s and HOR_S=60s instead of 10s (user request). Everything else byte-identical to dir10-20260712_cl_chain: same episodes rule (entry q90/q99, continuation q50/=entry, same-sign), same signals {f62 OBI_L1, COMP}, same year/symbols, forward returns = the SAME saved R/RV tensors at h=30s/60s ([H-2,H] window), next-tick tolerance 2s unchanged, MAXK=30 steps. Script change = env HOR_S parameterization only (R[HIDX], step target dtd+HOR_S). Comparison metrics vs the 10s cell: bp/episode total, added-by-chaining, per-SECOND capture efficiency (bp/s of hold time), chain length distribution, stop reasons. Expectation from the screen's horizon decay (IC halves 5->15s but cumulative capture grows mildly): longer quanta should capture more bp per episode at lower per-second efficiency and shorter chains; where the crossover sits is the question. Artifacts {SYM}_chain_h30.npz / _h60.npz.", "priority_rank": 1, "note": "Runs on dir10-1 from saved artifacts; ~4 min/horizon."}
