{"hypothesis_id": "HD5", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-07-12T12:10:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "h1fixedtau-20260712_cl_year", "statement": "HD5 - user hypothesis 1 (BTC/ETH expansion program): FIXED confidence threshold instead of the dynamic causal tau. RULE (user-specified, frozen before run): per walk-forward fold, validation window = last KDAYS=30 train days (the same window that seeds the deployed rolling tau); collect the post-factum per-day TOP-K scores on that window (K=5 for budget t5, K=10 for t10); tau_fixed = MEAN of all collected top-K scores; on the fold's 30-day test window select score >= tau_fixed FROZEN (no daily adaptation; day-count selectivity becomes variable, zero-trade days allowed). MOTIVATION: user recalls a prior selectivity-policy sweep where a hardcoded threshold strongly raised EV/tr at reduced trade count; targets = BTC, ETH (weak cells under the deployed policy), DOGE, XRP as references. DATA: rev8/s22 PERFOLD artifacts (anchored h150, 4 seeds x 6 folds), pure re-analysis, no retraining. VARIANTS: per-seed (4) and ENSEMBLE (mean rank-score, majority-vote side - ens_sym.py methodology); baseline = dynamic causal tau computed from the SAME artifacts with the same code path (sel_dyn == ens_sym causal semantics). METRICS (the surface): EV/tr, trades/day, bp/day = EV*tpd (the economic total - the fixed policy trades fewer, so bp/day decides), hit, per-fold breakdown, zero-trade-day share; ensemble cells get the REQUIRED perturbation gate for BOTH policies (sd .02/.05 x 100 reps). Headline = the (EV/tr, tpd, bp/day, jitter-robustness) surface of FIXED vs DYNAMIC per symbol; no binary verdict; deploy question (if any) is a separate later step per HM1 S5. Script scripts/subs60_h1_fixedtau.py.", "priority_rank": 1, "note": "Runs on dir10-1 (restart), 4 units SYMS={SYM}; ~1h wall (jitter-dominated); artifacts research_runs/h1_fixedtau/{SYM}_h1.json. Known caveat recorded up front: tau_fixed = mean of top-K > K-th-best cutoff -> expected tpd < K by construction; the K=5 dynamic-vs-fixed comparison is policy-vs-policy, not tpd-matched."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD5", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-07-12T13:05:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "h1fixedtau-20260712_cl_year_FIXQ_AMEND", "statement": "HD5 rev1 AMENDMENT (preregistered after the base tables of the primary run, before its jitter completion; motivated by the observed failure mechanism, spec frozen before the amendment run): the literal user rule (tau = MEAN of val-window per-day top-K scores) over-selects 30-65 trades/day instead of <=K because the AxB score is a product of TRAIN-referenced rank-CDFs - test scores saturate/clip at 1.0 and the count of clipped windows drifts by regime, so an absolute threshold near the top of the train scale is structurally unstable. To separate the user's actual question (STATIC hardcoded threshold vs DAILY-ADAPTIVE tau) from this scale artifact, add variant FIXQ: tau_fixed = the val-window (last 30 train days) quantile matched to K/day selectivity (q = 1 - K/wpd over the pooled val scores), FROZEN for the whole 30-day fold test - a hardcoded number with no daily adaptation, on the same scale the dynamic policy uses for its day-1 seed. FIXQ vs DYN difference then isolates the value of intra-test daily adaptation of the threshold. Same artifacts, metrics, jitter gate as the primary run; output {SYM}_h1v2.json (primary {SYM}_h1.json preserved).", "priority_rank": 1, "note": "Units h1q-{SYM} on dir10-1 AFTER the primary units finish (no concurrent duplicate-symbol runs)."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD5", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-07-12T14:30:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "h1fixedtau-20260712_cl_year", "statement": "HD5 rev1 MEASURED - STATIC-THRESHOLD SELECTIVITY SURFACE (two policy forms x 4 symbols x t5/t10, ensemble scoring, CL year, PERFOLD re-analysis; dynamic causal tau = baseline, reproduced exactly: DOGE +13.35/XRP +12.68/ETH +7.36/BTC +3.83 t5). (1) LITERAL USER RULE (tau = MEAN of val-window per-day top-K scores): structurally broken on this score parameterization - AxB test scores clip at 1.0 (train-referenced rank-CDF product) and the clipped-count drifts by regime, so the near-top absolute threshold over-selects 32-60 tr/day instead of <=K; EV/tr collapses (ENS t5: BTC -0.67, ETH -1.72, XRP -1.83, DOGE +1.33 with jitter sd.05 P76). (2) FIXQ FORM (tau = val-window quantile matched to K/day, FROZEN per 30-day fold test - the honest static-vs-adaptive test): the static threshold RETIMES rather than reduces trading - zero-trade days 69-86%, trades concentrate ~15-30% of days at ~15-20/day, total n ~= DYN. WHERE IT WINS: DOGE t5 +17.07 EV/tr (bpd +55.7 vs +44.5, hit 68.8%), jitter sd.02 p50 +7.46 P100 / sd.05 +2.92 P100 - matches DYN robustness while beating base EV by +3.7bp; DOGE t10 +10.51 (bpd +74.9 vs +61.5) P100/P100; XRP t5 +21.31 base (bpd +52.4 vs +39.2) but jitter-degraded to p50 +3.64 (=DYN) at sd.02 and MORE fragile at sd.05 (P7 vs P41); XRP t10 +6.91 P99. WHERE IT LOSES: the expansion targets - BTC t5 +2.25 vs +3.83 (t10 +0.09 vs +2.20), ETH t5 +5.08 vs +7.36 (t10 -0.79 vs +3.64), jitter no better. READING: a frozen bar auto-concentrates trading into high-score regimes; on thin-book symbols where score level carries regime information (DOGE/XRP) that concentration IS alpha (the user-remembered EV/tr boost, confirmed); on BTC/ETH score level does not translate across regimes and the static bar just starves good months. HYPOTHESIS-1 DOES NOT FIX BTC/ETH. Secondary deploy note (separate question): DOGE FIXQ t5/t10 is the only cell passing the full jitter battery while beating the deployed policy's base EV - candidate for a future recorder cross-check, NOT actioned.", "priority_rank": 1, "note": "Artifacts research_runs/h1_fixedtau/{SYM}_h1.json (literal rule) + {SYM}_h1v2.json (adds FIXQ); units h1-{SYM}, h1q-{SYM} on dir10-1; VM stopped. Caveats: FIXQ recalibrates at each fold boundary (monthly), not year-frozen; z0d 0.7-0.86 means realized capital utilization differs strongly from DYN - portfolio/occupancy implications unmeasured; per-seed FIXQ not summarized here (in jsons)."}
