{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 11, "ts": "2026-07-16T07:05:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "xgb-sobol-v2-BRIDGE_AMEND2_ISOLATION", "statement": "HD3 rev11 ISOLATION RESULT - the criterion-(b) deviation is SEARCH-DRIVEN, and the isolation came out maximally clean: SEARCH_MODE=tpe v2 (TPE search + QDM finals + inplace_predict + RAM diet) reproduced the v1 reference cells EXACTLY - seed0 +1.10 (perfold [4.7,5.4,-3.5,0.9,0.5,-2.8] == v1 seed0 to every reported digit, hit 58.1%), seed2 +15.01 (== v1 seed2, hit 68.7%). Spread seed2-seed0 = +13.92bp >= 6bp same-sign (prespecified read) -> the QuantileDMatrix/inplace_predict/RAM-diet path is not merely exonerated, it is RESULT-IDENTICAL to v1's DMatrix path on these cells; the ONLY source of v1<->v2 divergence is the search design (Sobol vs TPE). Therefore v2's tighter seed-sd (1.80 vs 6.32) = removal of TPE-trajectory noise, which was the DOMINANT component of v1 seed variance on this cell; residual v2 seed variance reflects data-subsample/xgb-seed noise. FOLD_PAR=6 demo: 66/66 PERFOLD arrays byte-equal to sequential (prereg requirement PASS); demo wall 35min vs 78min sequential. ADOPTION PROPOSAL (per AMEND2, decision = user review): adopt subs60_xgb_sobol_v2.py (Sobol mode) as PROTOCOL v2 for future tiers - all conclusion-level criteria pass, the one tripped bound was mis-calibrated for an intended variance-reduction; CALIBRATION CAVEATS to carry into v2 usage: (i) v2 seed-sd is NOT comparable to v1 seed-sd - seed-gates of the form mean-sd must be recalibrated or interpreted at the ensemble level (ens cells v1<->v2 agree: +12.27 vs +12.59); (ii) v2 cells ledger-tagged v2, never mixed with v1 cells in seed-sd comparisons. Speed (measured): x2.4-2.7 wall/job at matched nthread, x1.9 RAM packing, FOLD_PAR bit-safe -> campaign-level ~x4.5-5 vs v1 (plus class-A build sharding x7 for dataset builds).", "note": "Artifacts maker_labels_tb3s_h150d_v2t/ (TPE isolation) + _v2bf/ (FOLD_PAR demo) + _v2b/ (bridge)