{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 11, "ts": "2026-07-16T07:40:00Z", "status": "adopted", "result_experiment_id": "xgb-sobol-v2-ADOPTION", "statement": "PROTOCOL v2 ADOPTED by explicit user decision 2026-07-16 (single word directive after full disclosure of the bridge 4/5 + isolation result). FROZEN: scripts/subs60_xgb_sobol_v2.py, md5 a751ec3fef8ff32302fbf80af9be6481 (LF/git). v2 = DEFAULT trainer for NEW tiers; v1 (subs60_xgb_optuna_ic.py) stays frozen for v1-comparable reruns. BINDING USAGE RULES (recorded in runtime/README): (i) v2 cells are ledger-tagged v2 and never compared to v1 cells on seed-sd (v2 removes TPE-trajectory noise: measured BTC h150d seed-sd 6.32 -> 1.80 at unchanged ensemble +12.27 <-> +12.59); mean-sd seed-gates require v2-native recalibration; cross-protocol comparisons at ensemble/conclusion level only. (ii) SEARCH_MODE=tpe exists for isolation only, never for production cells. (iii) Any future change to v2 re-passes the bridge ritual. Orchestrator support: orchestrate2.py XSYM_TRAINER env (default v1 for backward compat). Measured throughput at adoption: x2.4-2.7 wall/job, x1.9 RAM packing, FOLD_PAR=6 bit-equal (35min/seed-run demo) -> rev10-class campaign ~3h vs ~14h; with class-A build sharding: full symbol-pair tier (build+train+ens) projected ~4h wall.", "note": "Bridge chain: xgb-sobol-v2-BRIDGE_PREREG (+AMEND1 cell switch, +AMEND2 isolation) -> BRIDGE measured (4/5, (b) miss 0.098bp in the improvement direction) -> ISOLATION measured (TPE-mode v2 == v1 exactly; divergence = search design only) -> user adoption. Artifacts: maker_labels_tb3s_h150d_v2b/, _v2t/, _v2bf/.", "priority_rank": 1}
