{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 13, "ts": "2026-07-16T09:50:00Z", "status": "annotated", "result_experiment_id": "economics3-20260716", "statement": "3-SYMBOL ECONOMICS (frozen economics.py methodology extended; artifacts research_runs/ECONOMICS_3sym_20260716.json; cells = year walk-forward test windows Dec25-May26, 163-169d, trade-level compounded, day-from-end alignment). Deployed 0.5-sizing per instance: DOGE FIXQ-t10 +12.0%/mo (Sharpe 4.86, tlDD -17.3%), XRP FIXQ-t5 +8.3%/mo (3.39, -8.3%), BTC DYN-t5 +5.1%/mo (2.12, -10.9%, worst day -4.9%, monthly buckets Dec+0.5/Jan+8.1/Feb+11.2/Mar+8.3/Apr+0.2/May+0.3, zero-days 80%). PORTFOLIO 3x0.5 as deployed: +27.0%/mo, Sharpe 4.85, trade-level maxDD -26.2% (1.5x gross of shared balance), zero-days 51%. Correlations (this methodology): DOGE-BTC +0.45 (dominant coupling, both winter-heavy), DOGE-XRP +0.12, XRP-BTC -0.06. DISCREPANCY FLAGGED: the 2-instance-era README reported DOGE-XRP +0.63 under FIXQ with different alignment/granularity, and its DD figures were shallower (likely daily-close vs trade-level) - reconciliation is an open item; cross-instance coupling treated as uncertain [0.1, 0.6]. Showcase README updated (dated 3-instance section, historical table kept in details). All numbers = edge densities at $10-1k notional; annualized figures are extrapolations of a 5.5-month window - capacity caveat binding.", "priority_rank": 2}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 14, "ts": "2026-07-16T10:21:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "tb3s-20260716_eth_levers_PREREG", "statement": "HD3 rev14 PREREG - ETH IN-CLASS LEVERS (exploratory surface; question: is ETH fixable INSIDE the h150 policy class, or does its alpha need a different class). Base cell = ETH x anchored honest (h150danch), protocol v2 (frozen a751ec3f). THREE levers, one campaign: (L1) REGIME GATE - offline re-analysis, no retrain: day-level causal activity gates applied to the DYN t5 selection of the rev12 v2 ens scores (gated-off days trade nothing, tau buffer still updates). Candidate features (prespecified, day-aggregates causal at day start from PRIOR days): (i) trailing-20d realized vol proxy = std of rH30 per day; (ii) trailing funding level |col13| day-mean percentile; (iii) trailing-5d mean of daily ens-score p99 (score-regime). Threshold grid per feature: gate-on when trailing value in {top,bottom} x {30,50,70}% of trailing-60d history. DELIVERABLE = the (feature x threshold) surface of EV/bpd/months vs ungated; MULTIPLE-TESTING HONESTY: 18 grid cells - argmax reported with LOFO(month) and flagged exploratory; any deploy use requires a fresh confirmatory prereg. (L2) 8-SEED ENSEMBLE - train v2 seeds 4-7 on h150danch (same protocol; OUT_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150danch_v2, extending rev12), 8-seed mean-rank ens (ens_sym generalized via SEEDS env, methodology otherwise identical) -> per-seed/ens/LOFO/jitter; question: does consensus cleaning push jitter P81 past the binding sd.02 gate. (L3) HOLD SWEEP - CFGIDX=0 (90s) and CFGIDX=2 (240s) x 4 seeds v2, OUT_SUB=..._v2c0/_v2c2 (labels already in the dataset); surface = per-seed+ens EV by hold; DOGE's 150s-peak was never measured on ETH. COST: 12 v2 jobs ~2h on xsym-32 + offline analysis, ~$6-8. NO deploy action from this rev; if all three levers fail to produce a binding-gate-passing cell, the recorded conclusion is 'ETH exits the h150 class' and the ETH thread moves to HD4 (sub-minute).", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "OPS-GATES", "rev": 2, "ts": "2026-07-16T12:53:00Z", "status": "decided", "result_experiment_id": "gate-policy-evolution-20260716", "statement": "GATE POLICY EVOLUTION (user decision 2026-07-16, follows the 2026-07-16 jitter-scale redefinition; user emphasis: REGIME STABILITY RANKS HIGHEST). Analysis that motivated it: jitter-P(EV>0) conflates three effects - (1) mechanical small-n dilution that grows with selectivity (measured: same BTC cell P100 at n=449 vs P86 at n=58; XRP P41 year vs P100 recorder) and thus systematically penalizes the very tail-selectivity that carries the alpha; (2) winner's-curse EV drop under score noise - real only across frames, and being engineered away by engine feature capture; (3) genuine overfit-to-marginal-windows - the only component the gate SHOULD catch, inseparable from (1)/(2) in the P>0 form. Historical failures were REGIME failures (ETH March, old-BTC May artifact), never jitter failures; the protections that worked = fold structure/LOFO, cross-frame consistency triangles, ensemble averaging, live acceptance parity. NEW BINDING GATE for deploy candidacy: (a) seed-gate (mean-sd>0, protocol-native scale); (b) REGIME STRUCTURE - fold/month table + LOFO (no deploy on cells carried by one regime; negative-regime months must be explainable/either excised by a preregistered causal gate or accepted explicitly); (c) DAY-BLOCK BOOTSTRAP (block L=7d, 1000 reps) on the test-day PnL series: CI90 on EV/tr and bpd, P(EV>0) >= 90% - honest estimator-uncertainty at any n, no anti-selectivity bias; (d) for cells measured on a FOREIGN frame (recorder gates of new instances): cross-frame p50-shift under measured-scale score perturbation reported as a DIAGNOSTIC (not pass/fail). Jitter P(EV>0) RETIRED from binding everywhere; printed as diagnostic. END STATE: new-instance gates move to SHADOW-CAPTURED windows of the instance's own stream (BTC acceptance = first such), after which (d) also retires. Applies to all future gates; past records not mutated.", "note": "Implementation: day-block bootstrap added to ens_sym battery (BOOT env, default on, orchestration layer); rev14 ETH cells re-adjudicated under the new gate in the rev14 measured record.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 15, "ts": "2026-07-16T13:44:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "eth_selectivity-20260716_PREREG", "statement": "HD3 rev15 PREREG - ETH SELECTIVITY-THRESHOLD FORMS + GATE CONFIRMATION (offline re-analysis of rev12+rev14 artifacts; no retrain, no VM cost). DATA: ETH x danch v2 PERFOLD seeds 0-7 + dataset npz labels (for causal payoff calibration). PART A - CONFIRMATORY (single prespecified test, no grid): the rev14-L1 argmax gate (scp99 trail-5d, gate-off when below bottom-30% of trailing-60d) re-evaluated on scores FULLY INDEPENDENT of its selection: ens of seeds 4-7 only (gate feature recomputed from those scores; DYN t5 selection on them). PASS = gated bpd >= ungated bpd AND day-block-bootstrap P(EV>0) >= 90% AND LOFO(month) min > 0 (OPS-GATES rev2 battery). PASS -> the gate is a real effect, candidate for the ETH deploy chain (recorder/shadow step next); FAIL -> gate written off as grid-selection artifact. PART B - EXPLORATORY SURFACE (8-seed ens scores, seeds 0-7; every cell reported with the rev2 battery: EV/n/bpd/months/LOFO/boot-CI90): threshold forms (1) DYN t5 reference; (2) DYN + scp99-gate; (3) DYN + HARDCODED score floor, grid X in {0.95,0.96,0.97,0.98,0.985,0.99}; (4) SEED-CONSENSUS floor: trade only when >=k of 8 per-seed scores clear their own fold-frozen t5-quantile, k in {4..8}; (5) EV-FLOOR: causal per-fold calibration E[net|ens score] on the last-30-train-day window (binned tail fit from dataset labels), trade when E_hat[net] >= X bp, X in {1,2,3,5}; (6) best-floor x gate combination. Multiple-testing honesty: part B is a surface (24+ cells) - its argmax is NOT a deploy claim; only part A carries confirmatory weight this rev, and any deploy proposal from part B requires its own prespecified confirmation (next rev or shadow window). Motivation thread: user hypothesis that score LEVEL carries regime information which quantile-DYN erases (supported: hit monotone in score demanded, FIXQ z0d self-throttling, scp99 gate) - the surface separates the level-usage forms: constant / trailing-normalized / consensus / economic-units.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 14, "ts": "2026-07-16T15:09:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "tb3s-20260716_eth_levers", "statement": "HD3 rev14 RESULT (prereg followed; all cells = ETH x danch x v2, OPS-GATES rev2 battery). L1 REGIME GATE: 18-cell surface showed real structure (edge concentrated in high-vol/high-score regimes; scp99-top70 argmax EV +13.7 bpd +23.9 BOOT-P99 on the 0-3 ens) BUT written off in rev15 Part A (see below). L2 8-SEED ENS: seeds 4-7 = [+17.9/-3.5/+4.4/+2.5] - genuine seed noise CONFIRMED huge (8-seed spread +-6.36, seed5 negative); 8-seed ens +8.60 (390tr, bpd +21.1, BOOT CI90 [+1.97,+17.14] P98, LOFO +5.23, jitter-diag P88) - marginal gain over 4-seed, consensus cleaning did NOT transform the cell; SEED-GATE at 8-seed scale FAILS (mean-sd = -0.34). L3 HOLD SWEEP - DOGE's 150s peak does NOT transfer cleanly: 90s = bpd +32.1 (740tr, best economics) but regime-fragile (March -13.2, LOFO +1.98, BOOT p5 +0.02); 240s = EV/tr +10.5 per-seed but ens BOOT P80 FAIL; 150s remains the balanced argmax under the full battery. Hold dimension is symbol/battery-conditional.", "note": "Artifacts maker_labels_tb3s_h150danch_v2{,c0,c2}/ + rev14_eth logs; 12 v2 jobs ~2.9h at 48-thread oversub; cost ~$8.", "priority_rank": 1}
