{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 19, "ts": "2026-07-18T22:40:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "tb3s-20260718_bnb_ltc_sol_honest_rebuild", "statement": "HD3 rev19 RESULT (prereg followed exactly; protocol v2.1 frozen 2a435f32, builder c90db57e, 4 seeds, t5, OPS-GATES rev2 batteries; all cells = symbol x CL-year(2025-05-09..2026-06-02, 365d, N~9M) x honest H5100 execution). PRIMARY - THE SURFACE (ENS t5 EV bp | per-seed mean+-sd | BOOT day-block P(EV>0) | jitter sd.02 P): BNB: anch -3.44 (-3.04+-1.67, P27) | true -0.34 (-0.14+-3.48, P54) | true x no-ToD +2.51 ARGMAX (625tr hit 56.6%, per-seed -1.32+-1.01, BOOT CI90 [-3.26,+9.08] P77, LOFO min -1.77 (fold1-carried), jitter.02 P36). LTC: anch -6.14 (P20) | true +1.21 ARGMAX (529tr, +1.23+-4.60, BOOT P64, jitter.02 P5) | true x no-ToD -4.09 (P30). SOL: anch -5.41 (P17) | true -0.11 ARGMAX (691tr, -5.75+-2.06 per-seed, BOOT P50, jitter.02 P16) | true x no-ToD -0.98 (P46, per-seed +0.58+-3.34). CONDITIONS DRIVING THE SURFACE: (1) TRUE FUNDING IS ARGMAX ON ALL THREE (ENS delta vs anch +3.1/+7.4/+5.3) - BTC's true-preference extends to every extension symbol; the deployed DOGE/XRP anchor semantics is wrong outside DOGE/XRP; live funding_rate col13 = top single Bg column on all three (8.9/8.6/8.3% gain). (2) ToD-ABLATION RESPONSE IS SYMBOL-CONDITIONAL: BNB +2.9 ENS (hit 47.9->56.6%), SOL ~0 ENS (per-seed +6.3), LTC -5.3 - the ETH doubling does NOT generalize, despite all three models being ETH-class clock-dominated (ToD 25.8/27.2/23.8% of Bg gain, 24 fold-models each, MODELS dumps parsed) => ToD gain-share does NOT predict the ablation response sign. (3) The rev8 negatives were NOT execution-horizon artifacts: book densities ~1.5/s => H1800 covered ~1200s >= the 510s the policy needs; matched-semantics anch cells moved little (BNB -3.00->-3.44, SOL -5.05->-5.41; LTC -10.77->-6.14 conflates H5100 + protocol v1->v2 - conclusion-level only). The improvement in this tier comes from funding semantics (+ ToD for BNB). (4) MAGNITUDES: argmax cells +2.51/+1.21/-0.11 vs deployed-class argmax +12..+16 (DOGE/XRP/BTC/ETH) - the h150 policy class harvests 5-10x less on BNB/LTC/SOL at every measured condition; seed-sd (v2 scale) 1.0-4.6. SECONDARY (deploy-gate annotation, labelled): NO cell approaches the binding gate (best BOOT P77 < 90, best jitter.02 P36-47, seed-gate mean-sd < 0 everywhere) - no deploy candidates, no capital action. FORWARD OPTIONS (not preregistered, user decision): (a) rev14/15 lever family on BNB-notod (8-seed, hardcoded/tau-floor, FIXQ); (b) hold sweep 90/240; (c) accept the surface and stop extension at the 4 deployed symbols.", "note": "Invocations: build unit h150d-build-ext2 (orchestrate v1, XSYM_TRAIN=0 XSYM_SUB_H=maker_labels_tb3s_h150d XSYM_SUB_A=maker_labels_tb3s_h150danch XSYM_H_TICKS=5100 XSYM_BUILD=BNB,LTC,SOL XSYM_BUILD_SHARDS=2), 09:56-10:49Z, EXC=0, 1095 dailies; stage1 units h150d-ext-train-{true,anch} (orchestrate2, XD split xd_true/xd_anch, XSYM_TRAINER=subs60_xgb_sobol_v2.py, NTHREAD=4, SLOTS 6+6, DATA_CACHE), 24 jobs ~7.3h; stage2 unit h150d-ext-train-notod (XSYM_OUT_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150d_v2notod, DROP_COLS=67,68,69,70, SLOTS=12), 12 jobs ~4.2h. VM xsym-32 total ~12.6h ~= $25 (scope $25-35), STOPPED 2026-07-18 22:33Z. Artifacts: h150d{,anch}/{BNB,LTC,SOL}.npz + daily x1095 + 36 SEED jsons + 216 PERFOLD + 576 MODELS dumps (v2.1 MODEL_DUMP, per user save-models directive) + 9 ENS jsons + rev19_logs.tgz (journal + all unit/job logs) in _v2notod/. Orchestration fixes shipped: orchestrate.py ANCH_SRC/DST passthrough (caught pre-launch: defaults would have rewritten rev8 h150anch), orchestrate2.py XSYM_OUT_SUB. Model anatomy (Bg gain families, all 3 symbols): ToD 24-27%, vol 11-14%, book/OBI 10-13%, liq 9-11%, funding 9-10% (col13 top), OI 6.5-8.5%, btc_lead ~1-2% - clock+carry context models like pre-ablation ETH.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 20, "ts": "2026-07-19T00:05:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "bnb_levers-20260719_PREREG", "statement": "HD3 rev20 PREREG - BNB LEVER DEEP-DIVE (user directive 2026-07-19: continue BNB with the remaining ETH levers that worked; SKIP jitter batteries to save wall time - BOOT day-block CI + LOFO + month structure remain the uncertainty measures). BASE CELL: BNB x true-funding x no-ToD (rev19 argmax: 4-seed ENS +2.51, BOOT P77). FROZEN SPEC: (L1) SEED EXTENSION - seeds 4-7 x BNB x maker_labels_tb3s_h150d x DROP_COLS=67,68,69,70 x protocol v2.1 (frozen 2a435f32), OUT_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150d_v2notod (extends rev19's 0-3); reads: (a) seeds 4-7 own 4-seed ens (draw confirmation, rev18 test-A form: same sign AND >= 50% of the 0-3 ens EV +2.51 -> draw-stable; both-negative -> rev19 argmax was draw luck), (b) pooled 8-seed ens + 8-seed seed-gate mean-sd (v2 scale), (c) 8-seed BOOT battery. (L2) SELECTIVITY FORMS (rev15 Part-B family, re-analysis of PERFOLD artifacts, no training): hardcoded score floors {0.97,0.98,0.985,0.99,0.995} x {4-seed 0-3, 4-seed 4-7, 8-seed} ens-score; causal TAU-FLOOR (trade only when trailing tau >= X, X in {0.95,0.96,0.97,0.98}); CONSENSUS floors (>=k of N seeds above own tau, k in {N/2..N}); reads: EV/tr, bpd, n, month table, LOFO(mo), BOOT CI - TREND-consistency required (monotone in the knob, not a grid spike); multiple-testing flag carried. (L3) DISJOINT HARMONY TEST (rev18 design verbatim): select by 4-7 ens / grade by 0-3 consensus AND symmetric; disagreement zone = 1-3 of 4 graders above own tau; read = EV(harmony) - EV(disagreement) in both directions (report, no 5bp bar - exploratory). DELIVERABLE: the BNB lever-response surface; deploy gate = secondary annotation (jitter component WAIVED by user directive, recorded here). COST: VM restart, 4 v2.1 jobs ~2.5-3h + local analysis ~= $6-8.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 20, "ts": "2026-07-19T03:30:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "bnb_levers-20260719", "statement": "HD3 rev20 RESULT (prereg followed; BNB x true x no-ToD, protocol v2.1, jitter WAIVED per user directive; span 163 test-days, BOOT day-block L=7x1000). L1 SEED EXTENSION: seeds 4-7 per-seed [+0.2/-0.7/-2.1/-2.6] ~= seeds 0-3 [-0.6/-2.3/-2.0/-0.3]; own 4-seed ens +0.12 - SAME SIGN but < 50% of the 0-3 ens (+2.51) -> DRAW CONFIRMATION FAIL: the rev19 4-seed DYN magnitude was draw-sensitive; 8-seed DYN ens +2.09 (740tr, bpd +9.51, BOOT P75) = the honest pooled level. POOLED SEED-GATE: mean-sd = -1.31-1.06 = -2.37 FAIL - per-seed EV is NEGATIVE on average; ALL positive economics on BNB lives in the ensemble layer (stronger form of the DOGE ensemble-dependence: there per-seed was positive-weak, here negative). L2 SELECTIVITY SURFACE (the campaign finding): CONSENSUS is BNB's working form, FLOOR/TAU-FLOOR are not (ETH's hardcoded-floor transfers negatively: floor 0.97-0.99 all negative, non-monotone; tau-floor <= +1.9). Consensus is MONOTONE in k on 8 seeds: >=4/8 -0.11 -> >=5/8 +1.33 -> >=6/8 +1.58 -> >=7/8 +5.91 (270tr, bpd +9.79 ~= full DYN bpd, hit 56.3%, LOFO(mo) +4.20, BOOT CI90 [-1.45,+17.72] P90, 0/6 negative months) -> 8/8 +10.05 (138tr, bpd +8.51, hit 59.4%, LOFO +6.63, CI90 [-0.76,+26.06] P94, 0 neg mo). Trend-consistent, not a grid spike; k-choice multiple-testing flag carried. L3 DISJOINT HARMONY (rev18 design): direction replicates BOTH ways - select 4-7/grade 0-3: harmony +1.70 vs disagreement -0.92 (gap 2.6bp); select 0-3/grade 4-7: +4.55 vs +0.25 (gap 4.3bp) - independent structural support for the consensus mechanism. READING: BNB has a REAL, structurally-supported, consensus-concentrated maker edge; its economics ceiling in this policy class = bpd ~+9.8 (consensus >=7/8) ~= +1.5-1.6%/mo at the 0.5 convention - ~5-8x below the deployed legs (DOGE +74.9 / XRP +52.4 / ETH +42.7 bpd). SECONDARY (deploy annotation, jitter waived): consensus->=7/8 sits AT the BOOT P>=90 bar with 0 negative months but fails the seed-gate (ensemble-only edge) and is economically marginal - NOT proposed for capital; standing = characterized reserve cell; possible continuations (user decision): recorder-EV cross-check of the consensus form as a 5th uncorrelated micro-leg, hold-sweep 90/240, or park.", "note": "Invocations: unit bnb-notod-s47 (orchestrate2, XSYM_JOBS=BNB:4..7, XSYM_OUT_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150d_v2notod, DROP_COLS=67-70, NTHREAD=6), 4 jobs ~2.1h, VM xsym-32 restart 00:15-02:50Z ~= $6, STOPPED. Analysis local: bnb_selectivity.py (session scratchpad; ens_sym-identical causal core, forms = floor/tau-floor/consensus, BOOT battery; no jitter per prereg). Artifacts: SEED4-7 jsons + 48 PERFOLD + 96 MODELS dumps appended to _v2notod/. Per-seed 8: [-0.6,-2.3,-2.0,-0.3,+0.2,-0.7,-2.1,-2.6].", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 20, "ts": "2026-07-19T05:10:00Z", "status": "annotated", "result_experiment_id": "bnb_levers-20260719_ADDENDUM_WR_SHARPE", "statement": "rev20 ADDENDUM (user question; same PERFOLD artifacts, same 163-day span, daily-PnL Sharpe ann sqrt(365), zero days included): CONSENSUS >=7/8: n=270, WR 56.3%, EV/tr +5.91, bpd +9.79, Sharpe 1.52, ACTIVE DAYS 18/163 (11%), worst day -436.8bp / best +1209.3bp. CONSENSUS 8/8: n=138, WR 59.4%, EV/tr +10.05, bpd +8.51, Sharpe 1.71, active 11/163 (7%), worst -224.8 / best +1003.1. READING: the consensus form is OCCUPANCY-CONCENTRATED (FIXQ-like: ~90% empty days, ~13-15 trades/day in high-consensus regime days) - the Sharpe is a rare-fat-days Sharpe with heavy single-day tails. Deployed-leg comparison (same year-WF methodology): DOGE 4.86 / XRP 3.39 / ETH 2.4-2.5 - BNB consensus at 1.5-1.7 is 2-3x below the weakest deployed leg; confirms reserve-cell standing.", "priority_rank": 2}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 21, "ts": "2026-07-19T05:40:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "bnb_nf10-20260719_PREREG", "statement": "HD3 rev21 PREREG - BNB VOL-GATE WIDTH LEVER (user directive 2026-07-19: same two consensus cells, but model A learns to catch the top-10%% most volatile moves instead of top-5%%). INTERPRETATION FIXED HERE: 'catch top 10%%' = the single conceptual dial vol-regime width = BOTH coupled constants NF_RATE 0.05->0.10 (A label: |rH| >= train-window q90 instead of q95) AND GATE_PCT 5->10 (the oof-pA gate zone B trains inside); attribution of the pair vs single-knob variants is OUT of this rev's scope. FROZEN PROTOCOL UNTOUCHED: variant = byte-copy trainer scripts/subs60_xgb_sobol_v2_nf10.py (md5 LF 6fb0171e2f963d9d9566c8b39c845de3, sole diff = the two constants, rev16 byte-copy precedent), NOT a protocol cell; artifacts to OUT_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150d_v2notod_nf10. RUN: BNB x maker_labels_tb3s_h150d (true) x DROP_COLS=67,68,69,70 x seeds 0-7 (8 jobs), CFGIDX=1 BUDGETS=5 SAVE_PF=1, MODEL_DUMP default-on. PRESPECIFIED READS (vs rev20 same-span baselines; NO jitter per standing user directive): (a) 8-seed DYN t5 ens (base +2.09 / bpd +9.51 / Sharpe-daily), (b) CONSENSUS >=7/8 (+5.91/bpd +9.79/WR 56.3/Sharpe 1.52) and 8/8 (+10.05/bpd +8.51/WR 59.4/Sharpe 1.71) - EV/tr, n, bpd, WR, LOFO(mo), month table, BOOT L=7x1000, daily Sharpe, occupancy; (c) monotonicity of the consensus ladder preserved y/n; (d) per-seed 8 EVs + pooled seed-gate. Success direction = bpd/Sharpe up at comparable BOOT-P (wider gate -> more trades; EV/tr may dilute - that alone is not failure). COST: VM restart, 8 v2-class jobs ~2.5h single wave ~= $6-8.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 21, "ts": "2026-07-19T09:20:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "bnb_nf10-20260719", "statement": "HD3 rev21 RESULT (prereg followed; BNB x true x no-ToD x NF10 variant trainer 6fb0171e (NF_RATE 0.10 / GATE_PCT 10), 8 seeds, same 163-day span, no jitter per standing directive). THE SURFACE vs rev20 NF5 baselines: per-seed mean -2.14 (NF5 -1.31); 8-seed DYN +0.62 / bpd +2.93 / BOOT P64 (NF5 +2.09 / +9.51 / P75); CONSENSUS >=7/8: +2.19 / bpd +3.58 / WR 52.8% / Sharpe 1.05 / P80 (NF5: +5.91 / +9.79 / 56.3% / 1.52 / P90); CONSENSUS 8/8: +6.69 / bpd +6.24 / WR 57.2% / Sharpe 2.13 / BOOT CI90 [+3.70,+13.79] P100 / LOFO(mo) +1.70 / months Jan +9.7%% dominant (NF5: +10.05 / +8.51 / 59.4% / 1.71 / CI90 [-0.76,+26.06] P94 / LOFO +6.63). READING: (1) WIDENING THE VOL GATE TO TOP-10%% DILUTES THE BNB EDGE - the harvestable signal is concentrated in the top-5%% vol regime; prespecified success direction (bpd/Sharpe up) FAILS on bpd everywhere and on Sharpe for >=7/8. (2) The consensus ladder stays MONOTONE under NF10 (4/8 -1.62 -> 8/8 +6.69) - the consensus mechanism is robust to the gate-width change, its LEVEL is not. (3) The one genuine NF10 gain: the 8/8 unanimity cell becomes SMOOTHER - Sharpe 1.71->2.13, first BNB cell with a fully positive BOOT CI90 (low +3.70, P100), at the price of ~27%% less bpd and heavier January-dependence (LOFO +1.70 vs +6.63 - one-month lean). SECONDARY (deploy annotation): still no capital case - NF10-8/8 bpd +6.24 ~= +1%%/mo @0.5, LOFO(mo) near zero; reserve standing unchanged; NF5 CONSENSUS remains BNB's best-economics form, NF10-8/8 its smoothest form.", "note": "Invocation: unit bnb-nf10 (orchestrate2, XSYM_TRAINER=subs60_xgb_sobol_v2_nf10.py, XSYM_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150d, XSYM_OUT_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150d_v2notod_nf10, DROP_COLS=67-70, 8 jobs NTHREAD=4 single wave ~2.6h), VM xsym-32 ~3.2h ~= $7, STOPPED. Per-seed EVs [-0.59,-3.26,-1.57,-1.41,-0.92,-3.13,-2.12,-4.12]. Artifacts: _v2notod_nf10/ 8 SEED jsons + 48 PERFOLD + 192 MODELS dumps. Analysis local bnb_selectivity.py on pf_nf10.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 21, "ts": "2026-07-19T11:00:00Z", "status": "annotated", "result_experiment_id": "consensus_xsym-20260719_ANNOT", "statement": "CROSS-SYMBOL CONSENSUS ANNOTATION (user hypothesis: 'seed-consensus = classic uncorrelated-ensemble theory, tendency should be universal across symbols'; re-analysis of existing PERFOLD artifacts at each symbol's argmax variant, no training: DOGE/XRP h150anch 4s, BTC h150d-true 4s, ETH danch-notod 8s, BNB h150d-true-notod 8s, LTC/SOL h150d-true 4s; BOOT 400 reps, no jitter). LAYER 1 - THE MECHANISM IS UNIVERSAL: pairwise seed score-corr 0.60-0.76 on every symbol, yet tail-selection (causal t5) Jaccard only 0.20-0.32 - seeds agree on scores but DISAGREE on the extreme tail; the decorrelation lives at the decision boundary, exactly the Condorcet-jury material. LAYER 2 - THE VALUE OF UNANIMITY IS SYMBOL-CONDITIONAL, tracking per-seed competence (Condorcet: majority amplifies accuracy only when jurors beat chance): DOGE cons 2/4->4/4: EV +11.8->+28.6, WR 63->77%, Sharpe peak 3.52 at >=3/4 (bpd +35.1); XRP: +10.3->+26.8, Sharpe peak 3.99 at >=3/4; BTC: peak >=3/4 +18.1 then flat, bpd decays fast; ETH: peak at >=6/8 (+24.5, bpd +36.3) then DECLINES to 8/8 (+17.2) - unanimity overshoots; BNB: monotone to 8/8 +10.05 (the rev20 finding); LTC: INVERTED - 4/4 NEGATIVE -5.83 (unanimous conviction unanimously wrong); SOL: only 4/4 weakly positive +4.23. READING: seed-consensus is a real, universal decorrelation structure whose SIGN follows the base per-seed edge (strong edge -> concentration, DOGE/XRP/BTC/ETH; weak/negative edge -> noise or inverted concentration, LTC/SOL); the user's universality prediction holds for the mechanism, not for the payoff. ACTIONABLE FLAG (not preregistered, hypothesis only): DOGE/XRP consensus >=3/4 gives EV/tr x1.7-2 vs deployed mean-score ens at ~70-80% bpd and Sharpe 3.5-4.0 - a potential future selectivity overlay for the deployed legs if capacity/fee conditions ever favor fewer-better trades; requires own prereg + FIXQ-comparison before any action.", "priority_rank": 2}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 21, "ts": "2026-07-19T12:30:00Z", "status": "annotated", "result_experiment_id": "bnb_roi_dd-20260719_ANNOT", "statement": "BNB ROI-vs-maxDD ANNOTATION (user question; economics convention @0.5 SIZE_FRAC, per-trade equity compounding, 163-day span, daily equity curve maxDD): NF5 DYN 8-seed: ROI/mo +1.41%, maxDD -9.45%, ratio 0.15; NF5 CONSENSUS >=7/8: +1.46%/mo, -4.00%, ratio 0.37; NF5 CONSENSUS 8/8: +1.28%/mo, -1.91%, ratio 0.67; NF10 CONSENSUS 8/8: +0.93%/mo, -1.50%, ratio 0.62. KEY READING: consensus does NOT trade ROI for drawdown - >=7/8 slightly BEATS DYN on ROI (+1.46 vs +1.41) while cutting maxDD 2.4x; 8/8 cuts DD 5x for ~9% ROI; ROI/|DD| monotone in consensus threshold (0.15->0.37->0.67). Deployed-leg scale (same convention): ETH no-ToD ~+4.9%/mo at -5.0% DD (ratio ~1.0) - best BNB form matches ETH-class curve QUALITY at ~4x lower absolute return; standing unchanged (micro-leg candidate pending recorder-EV, or park).", "priority_rank": 2}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 22, "ts": "2026-07-19T14:40:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "bnb_budget_regime-20260719", "statement": "HD3 rev22 (free tier: re-analysis of existing artifacts, no training; BNB x true x no-ToD 8-seed, 163d span). PART 1 - SELECTIVITY-BUDGET SURFACE (tau target sweep, exploratory grid t10/t5/t2.5/t1, MONOTONE - not a spike): DYN t10 -1.94 (bpd -17.3) / t5 +2.09 (+9.5) / t2.5 +4.88 (+10.4) / t1 +12.79 (159tr, bpd +12.48, WR 64.8%, LOFO(mo) +9.06, BOOT CI90 [+5.69,+19.16] P99, Sharpe 2.94, Sortino 11.2, ROI/mo @0.5 +1.88%, maxDD -1.17%, 0/5 neg months). DRAW CONFIRMATION (rev18 form): t1 replicates on BOTH independent 4-seed draws - seeds 0-3 +12.12 (bpd +10.56) / seeds 4-7 +8.95 (bpd +12.02) - FIRST BNB lever to pass the draw test at full magnitude (t2.5 is draw-sensitive: +6.60 vs +0.99). READING: the BNB edge is an EXTREME-TAIL phenomenon; at t5 it was diluted by ~4 net-negative trades/day; consensus was a proxy for the same concentration (t1 DYN needs no consensus). REALIZED OCCUPANCY: 159 trades in 14 active days (~11/day bursts, FIXQ-like) - t1 is a TARGET, not a daily rate. CAVEATS: budget grid chosen post-hoc (multiple testing, mitigated by monotonicity + draw replication); t1 outside the t5/t10 deploy-scope convention; n=159. PART 2 - REGIME ANATOMY (per-day aggregates from BNB.npz F cols): t1-active days = elevated short-horizon rv (+0.54sd), OI-deltas (+0.3sd), POSITIVE mean funding (+0.35sd), liq-neutral; LOSING trades sit on the MOST extreme rv days (+0.98sd). EV monotone in day liq-intensity quartile: Q1 +8.5 -> Q4 +29.0 (n=16) - supports the liq-conditionality hint from model anatomy (liq family 11.4% gain). JANUARY DEMYSTIFIED: jan is LOW-vol (-0.48sd rv), liq-quiet (-0.45sd), but funding-elevated (+0.53sd) - the edge month is a carry regime, not a vol regime. NEXT-STEP MENU (user decision): (a) prereg + recorder-stream inventory for a BNB DYN-t1 recorder-EV cross-check (the micro-deploy path); (b) liq/OI ablations + hold sweep (VM, ~$10-15) to try lifting the base per-seed edge; (c) t-budget sweep on other symbols' existing PERFOLDs (free) to test lever generality.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 23, "ts": "2026-07-19T15:20:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "bnb_liq_oi_ablation-20260719_PREREG", "statement": "HD3 rev23 PREREG - BNB LIQ/OI FEATURE-FAMILY ABLATIONS (ETH rev17 template; user-directed continuation; goal = lift the NEGATIVE per-seed BASE edge so wider budgets (t2.5-t5, n=350-740) turn positive => statistical power without dilution). BASE: BNB x maker_labels_tb3s_h150d (true) x no-ToD. RUNS (protocol v2.1 frozen 2a435f32, 4 seeds each, CFGIDX=1 BUDGETS=5 SAVE_PF=1): (V1) no-ToD+no-LIQ: DROP_COLS=19,43,56,57,58,67,68,69,70 -> OUT_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150d_v2notod_noliq; (V2) no-ToD+no-OI: DROP_COLS=59,60,67,68,69,70 -> OUT_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150d_v2notod_nooi. COMPETING HYPOTHESES the ablation separates: (a) liq/OI = noisy crutch (non-recurring cascade patterns overfit the year) -> base rises (ETH scenario); (b) liq/OI = real signal (supported by rev22 EV-monotone-in-liq-intensity Q1 +8.5 -> Q4 +29) -> base falls, liq-conditionality confirmed causally -> motivates regime conditioning instead of ablation. PRESPECIFIED READS (no jitter, per standing directive): per-seed mean vs baseline (-1.32+-1.01 seeds 0-3 notod), 4-seed DYN ens at t5 (+2.51 baseline) and the t-budget surface t5/t2.5/t1 per variant (baseline t1 +12.79 8-seed / +12.12 seeds 0-3); month table + BOOT battery. CONTINUATION RULE (prespecified): a variant with per-seed mean > 0 OR DYN t5 ens > +5 gets seeds 4-7 for draw confirmation before any further claim. COST: VM restart, 8 v2-class jobs single wave ~2.5h ~= $7.", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HD3", "rev": 23, "ts": "2026-07-20T02:20:00Z", "status": "measured", "result_experiment_id": "bnb_liq_oi_ablation-20260719", "statement": "HD3 rev23 RESULT (prereg followed; BNB x true x no-ToD base, 4 seeds each, protocol v2.1, no jitter). V1 no-LIQ (drop 19,43,56-58): per-seed -1.88+-0.64 (baseline -1.32+-1.01), DYN t5 -0.60 (baseline +2.51), t2.5 +2.21, t1 +7.88 BOOT-P99 (baseline +12.12) - degrades everywhere, tail survives weakened. V2 no-OI (drop 59,60): per-seed -2.48+-0.73, DYN t5 -1.63, t2.5 +0.57, t1 +0.45 P56 - the TAIL EDGE COLLAPSES ENTIRELY. CONTINUATION RULE: neither variant triggered (per-seed<0, t5<+5 both) - no seeds 4-7. READING: (1) hypothesis (a) 'noisy crutch' REFUTED for both families - BNB's weak base is NOT an ETH-style feature-poison problem; (2) OI-DELTAS (cols 59-60, ~7.5min/75min positioning change) ARE THE LOAD-BEARING CARRIER of the t1 tail edge - removing them kills it (consistent with x60 top-3 anatomy column and rev22 active-day profile rv+/OI+/funding+); liq family is secondary signal (EV-monotone-in-liq-intensity survives via correlated OI/rv, tail alive at +7.88 without liq); (3) the BNB edge mechanism is now characterized: POSITIONING-BURST phenomenon (OI-delta bursts + liq intensity + positive-funding carry) harvested at extreme selectivity; base dilution at t5 is trades OUTSIDE these bursts - not removable by feature ablation. PATHS LEFT to statistical power (user decision): (i) hold-sweep 90/240 (different time constant may widen the edge zone); (ii) preregistered causal regime-conditioning (wider budget gated by OI/liq-activity - the family that failed OOS for ETH, requires strict out-of-selection design); (iii) accumulate live data (recorder BNB streams) and revisit; (iv) accept DYN t1 (n=159, both-draws-replicated) as the terminal in-year form.", "note": "Invocation: units bnb-abl-noliq/-nooi (orchestrate2 XSYM_OUT_SUB, 4+4 jobs NTHREAD=4, ~2.6h), VM xsym-32 ~3.1h ~= $7, STOPPED. Artifacts: _v2notod_noliq/ + _v2notod_nooi/ (8 SEED jsons, 48 PERFOLD, 192 MODELS dumps). Analysis local (tau target 5/2.5/1).", "priority_rank": 1}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-08-06T12:05:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_bybit_doge_h150anch_repl_PREREG", "priority_rank": 1, "summary": "Frozen spec BEFORE running. QUESTION (exploratory venue-axis characterization): does the deployed DOGE anchored-h150 policy's alpha surface reproduce when the ONLY substantive change is the venue/data-source \u2014 free Bybit linear archives (quote-saver ob500->2025-08-20->ob200 L2 stream replay top-20 @~10/s; public.bybit.com tick trades) replacing the paid CL Binance feed (GCS dead since 2026-08-05 billing closure)? Window/protocol identical to tb3s-20260709_h150anch_year_4seeds: START=2025-05-09 END=2026-06-02, SYMF=DOGE-USDT-PERP FULLFEAT=1 ENTRY_MS=60000 HOLDS_S=90,150,240 CHASE_MS=300000 STEP_S=3, H_TICKS=5100 (path length scaled to ~10/s Bybit density per rev10 dense-book precedent; time windows unchanged). FROZEN measurement layer byte-identical (md5: build c90db57e5289a346fc241776a89cfa21, sobol_v2 2a435f32e2517479e0232260c85aad1a, prep_anch a1c3663de1d2e5286ce16806dfbfa5ed, ens_sym 9bf89832f0dca3eef4f0dc35c169ea33, perseed 3f6af11f5649a2d3a0cd5f4a67a81fc5); storage IO redirected by a google.cloud.storage local-FS shim (research/runtime/bybit_repl/gcs_shim, LOCAL_GCS_ROOT on a Modal Volume) \u2014 no frozen-script edits. Bins per bins.sh: fb from this branch rust_ingest, build_samples+grid_sim_exitdbg from origin/claude/husdc-rev1 ae2d871 + frozen bin sources. Training PROTOCOL v2 (default for new tiers; cross-protocol comparison at ensemble/conclusion level only per v2 rules): CFGIDX=1 BUDGETS=5,10 seeds 0-3 SAVE_PF=1 PFTAG=_S{s} MODEL_DUMP=1, anchored dataset via prep_anch_sym ANCH_MODE=anchor, ensemble via ens_sym.py. PRE-DECLARED DEVIATIONS (free-data gaps, all ledger-visible): (1) funding = Binance settled-rate venue-proxy on 1-min grid, causal last-settled<=t; mark_price = Bybit 1-min trade price (col44 zeroed by anchor anyway); (2) open_interest = Binance metrics