{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 1, "ts": "2026-08-06T12:35:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_bybit_doge_h150anch_repl_PREREG_AMEND1", "summary": "AMEND1 (before any production build): Modal-egress probe shows api.bybit.com IS reachable from the compute (geo-fence only hits the dev container) -> deviations (1) funding and (2) open_interest are UPGRADED from Binance-Vision venue-proxies to the REAL Bybit venue: funding = /v5/market/funding/history settled rates (causal last-settled<=t on the 1-min grid, unchanged construction), OI = /v5/market/open-interest 5min. Binance-Vision path retained as automatic fallback, actual source recorded in bybit_aux/sources.json. Remaining deviations unchanged: liquidations absent, BTC-lead = trade-price proxy, 5min OI granularity vs CL ~4s.", "note": "probe: archive HTTP 200, rest HTTP 200 (modal app ap-adBGhSS7C2rz93sgcr7LDZ)."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 2, "ts": "2026-08-06T15:40:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_bybit_doge_h150anch_V1PROTO_PREREG", "summary": "Frozen spec BEFORE running. QUESTION: how much of the ensemble-amplification gap in rev1 (CL ens/per-seed 1.64x vs Bybit-v2 0.55x) is PROTOCOL (v2 deterministic Sobol removing TPE-trajectory seed diversity) vs venue/data? Run: PROTOCOL v1 subs60_xgb_optuna_ic.py BYTE-UNCHANGED (sequential per-fold Optuna TPE 25 trials, FOLD_PAR=1, seeds 0-3, CFGIDX=1, BUDGETS=5,10, SAVE_PF=1 PFTAG=_S{s}, NTHREAD=5) on the IDENTICAL rev1 Bybit dataset copied to NEW prefix research_runs/maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch_v1/ (append-only: rev1 v2 artifacts untouched). Analysis: perseed_from_pf + ens_sym + t-surface {1,2,3,5,10,20} via XSYM_SUB. PRIMARY deliverable: the v1-protocol Bybit surface (per-seed sd, ties pct, ensemble EV by budget) alongside rev1-v2. Attribution reading pre-declared: if v1 ens/per-seed ratio recovers toward CL 1.64x, the rev1 ensemble gap is protocol-driven (seed diversity); if it stays ~0.5-0.6x, it is venue/data-driven (liq/OI/microstructure). Same-protocol comparison v1-Bybit vs v1-CL (tb3s-20260709: per-seed t5 +8.14+-2.55, ENS +13.35, ties 15.9 pct) is then apples-to-apples. Compute: Modal virginship07, est 11-14 USD (4x cpu5/18GiB x 2.5-3h), within the 30 USD grant (3.75 spent)."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 3, "ts": "2026-08-06T16:10:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_bybit_doge_nooi_ablation_PREREG", "summary": "Frozen spec BEFORE running (runs PARALLEL to rev2 v1-protocol, independent artifact prefixes). QUESTION: is the 5-min venue-OI proxy (deviation (2) of rev1: Bybit REST 5min vs CL ~4s) carrying signal or injecting noise into the Bybit cell? RUN: protocol v2.1 frozen 2a435f32, 4 seeds, CFGIDX=1 BUDGETS=5,10 SAVE_PF=1 PFTAG=_S{s} MODEL_DUMP=1, dataset UNCHANGED maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch, DROP_COLS=59,60 (the OI-delta family per HD3 rev23 canon), OUT_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch_v2_nooi. no-LIQ variant NOT run: liq inputs are absent on Bybit so cols 19/43/56-58 are already dead - the ablation would be inert by construction. COMPETING HYPOTHESES: (a) coarse-OI = noise -> surface RISES without it; (b) OI-deltas = real carrier (BNB rev23 analog: t1 +12.12 -> +0.45 without them) -> tail collapses; (c) inert on DOGE. PRESPECIFIED READS vs rev1 baseline: per-seed t5 mean vs +9.15+-6.28, ens t5 vs +5.06, ens t-surface t1/t2/t3 vs +17.84/+11.27/+8.71. Cost ~3 USD Modal virginship07 (parallel with rev2; combined projection ~20 USD of the 30 grant)."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 4, "ts": "2026-08-06T17:45:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_union_policy_PREREG", "summary": "Frozen spec BEFORE running (analysis-only on rev1 PERFOLD artifacts, ~0.1 USD). POLICY: UNION-of-seeds aggregation \u2014 each of 4 seeds runs the frozen causal_rolling on its own scores at per-seed target T_s in {1.25,2.5,5}/day; union traded once per decision; side = majority of SELECTING seeds (ties skipped, rate reported); fills/nets from fold artifacts unchanged. Motivated by the traded-tail diversity measurement (hbv1-...traded_tail_diversity): k=1 single-seed exclusives carry +19.4bp and are structurally discarded by the mean-rank ensemble. BATTERY (standing no-jitter directive per HD3 rev20): EV/tr, tpd, hit, per-fold sums, 30-day month buckets, day-block BOOT L=7 x1000 CI90 + P(EV>0), consensus-k decomposition. PRESPECIFIED comparison points: mean-rank ens t5 +5.06 (5.9/d) / t10 -0.56 (10/d); bucket-based union projection ~+11.4bp at ~10.8/d (T_s=5). READ RULE: union is interesting if EV/tr at comparable tpd beats the mean-rank ens AND BOOT P(EV>0)>=90% AND the edge is not single-fold; otherwise record the surface and stop."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 6, "ts": "2026-08-06T20:45:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_nooi_x_union_PREREG", "summary": "Frozen spec BEFORE running (analysis-only on the rev3 _v2_nooi PERFOLD artifacts). QUESTION: do the two measured improvements STACK \u2014 no-OI (per-seed t5 +9.15->+14.40, coarse-OI noise removed) x union aggregation (does not discard k=1 exclusives)? RUN: union_policy.py (same battery: no jitter, per-fold, 30d months, day-block BOOT L=7 x1000, consensus-k) at T_s in {1.25,2.5,5} on XSYM_SUB=maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch_v2_nooi. PRESPECIFIED comparison points: v2-base union +20.91/+16.37/+11.38 at 4.1/6.5/10.1 tpd; v1 union +30.42/+23.84/+13.71; nooi mean-rank ens t5 +4.76 / t1 +26.37. READ RULE: stacking confirmed if nooi-union > v2-base union at matched T_s with BOOT P>=90%; fold structure reported either way."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 7, "ts": "2026-08-06T21:20:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_8seed_nooi_unions_PREREG", "summary": "Frozen spec BEFORE running (user-directed). RUNS: (a) v1-protocol x no-OI, seeds 0-7 \u2014 subs60_xgb_optuna_ic.py BYTE-UNCHANGED, DROP_COLS=59,60, dataset copy in NEW prefix maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch_v1_nooi (append-only), CFGIDX=1 BUDGETS=5,10 SAVE_PF=1 PFTAG=_S{s} FOLD_PAR=1 NTHREAD=5; (b) v2-protocol x no-OI seeds 4-7 appended to the existing _v2_nooi prefix (same spec as rev3). ANALYSES on completion: 8-seed UNION battery (union_policy.py SEEDS=0..7, no-jitter, TGTS 0.625/1.25/2.5/5 \u2014 0.625 added because an 8-member union at fixed T_s roughly doubles tpd vs 4 members) on BOTH prefixes; 8-seed mean-rank ens via ens_sym SEEDS env as secondary annotation. PRESPECIFIED comparison points (4-seed): nooi-v2-union +24.19/+16.96/+14.69 at T1.25/2.5/5; v1-union +30.42/+23.84/+13.71; ens references rev2/3. READ: does doubling N thicken the harvestable union tail at matched tpd (EV at ~3-4/d and ~10/d vs the 4-seed forms), and does the k>=3 consensus-carried structure of nooi persist at N=8? Est cost ~8 USD (12 train jobs), spend before run ~9.6 of 30."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 8, "ts": "2026-08-06T21:40:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_xproto_union_PREREG", "summary": "Frozen spec BEFORE running (analysis-only, ~0.05 USD; runs while rev7 trains). QUESTION: does CROSS-PROTOCOL union (v1 TPE seeds + v2 Sobol seeds as one 8-member pool) beat same-protocol unions at matched tpd \u2014 i.e. is protocol heterogeneity a real diversity source on the traded tail (heterogeneous-ensemble theory)? RUN: union_policy.py MEMBERS mode, 8 members = maker_labels_tb3s_h150anch:{0..3} (v2 base) + _v1:{0..3} (v1), TGTS 0.625/1.25/2.5/5, same no-jitter battery. Fold/label compatibility: both protocols trained on the SAME dataset -> identical folds/days/nets (verified by construction). PRESPECIFIED comparisons: v2-base union +20.91/+16.37/+11.38 and v1 union +30.42/+23.84/+13.71 at T1.25/2.5/5 (4 members each; note an 8-member union at T_s has ~2x the tpd of a 4-member one \u2014 compare at matched TPD, e.g. xproto T0.625 vs 4-member T1.25). READ: xproto beats BOTH same-protocol unions at matched tpd => protocol diversity adds harvestable tail; matches only the better one => v1 diversity subsumes; worse => protocols disagree destructively (side conflicts)."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 8, "ts": "2026-08-06T21:55:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_xproto_union", "summary": "CROSS-PROTOCOL UNION SURFACE (prereg followed; 8 members = v2-base seeds 0-3 + v1 seeds 0-3, no-jitter battery). T0.625: +31.15bp, 613tr, 3.3/d, hit 62.3%, BOOT CI90 [+5.38,+70.81] P100. T1.25: +26.65, 4.9/d, P99. T2.5: +19.71, 8.2/d, P98, CI90 [+1.78,+44.64]. T5: +12.15, 13.5/d, P94. Ties 0.0-0.1% (protocols do NOT conflict on side). MATCHED-TPD READ (prereg): at ~3.3/d xproto +31.2 ~= v1-union +30.4 (hit better, 62.3 vs 60.0); at ~8/d xproto +19.7 CLEARLY beats v1-union-T5 +13.7 @11.3/d and nooi-union-T5 +14.7 @9.7/d -> protocol heterogeneity IS an additive diversity source on the traded tail (heterogeneous-ensemble mechanism), strongest in the mid-tpd range. Consensus-k at N=8 mixed (k=1/k=2 strong, k=8 solid +16..+31) \u2014 no monotone structure; fold2 still carries the bulk. BEST MEASURED FORMS by tpd band now: ~3/d xproto T0.625 +31.2 (floor +5.4) or v1-union +30.4; ~8/d xproto T2.5 +19.7 (floor +1.8); ~10/d nooi-union T5 +14.7 (floor +2.5). PENDING (after rev7): the stacked 16-member xproto-nooi union (v1-nooi 0-7 + v2-nooi 0-7) \u2014 the combination of every confirmed improvement.", "note": "Artifact HBV1_UNION_DOGE_xproto8.json (anch prefix). Analysis-only, ~0.05 USD."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 9, "ts": "2026-08-06T22:15:00Z", "status": "preregistered", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_validity_gate_REAUDIT_PREREG", "summary": "STANDING VALIDITY GATE (user directive 2026-08-06, binding for all HBV1+ deploy-relevant claims): a form is INVALID if ANY of: (a) at least one negative fold; (b) the magnitude is concentrated in a single period (operational test: LOFO by fold \u2014 excluding the best fold must leave a materially positive EV, as in the deployed CL cell where LOFO-fold2 kept +10.9 of +13.35); (c) day-block BOOT CI90 floor ~0 or below. Rationale: no deployed cell has any of these; year-scale forms that ride one burst period are not policies. Consequence for the current record: most rev4/6/8 union headline numbers are hereby RECLASSIFIED as burst-characterization surfaces, not deploy candidates; the re-audit under this gate follows as a measured record. union_policy.py extended to emit per-fold n/EV + LOFO so the gate is computable for union forms."}
{"hypothesis_id": "HBV1", "rev": 9, "ts": "2026-08-06T22:45:00Z", "status": "measured", "experiment_id": "hbv1-20260806_validity_gate_REAUDIT", "summary": "VALIDITY-GATE RE-AUDIT of all HBV1 forms (prereg followed; gate = user directive: no negative fold, no single-period concentration [LOFO by fold], BOOT floor materially > 0). RESULT \u2014 exactly ONE form passes ALL three criteria: **no-OI x union T_s=1.25: +24.19bp/tr, 617tr, 3.3/d, hit 58.0%; per-fold per-trade EV ALL positive [+40.8/+37.2/+66.5/+6.2/+18.4/+7.3/+55.1]; LOFO-min +13.98 (dropping the BEST fold keeps 58% of EV \u2014 the CL deployed standard kept 82%); BOOT CI90 [+7.81,+41.66] P100**. Honest annotation: folds 0/4/6 are thin (n=1/14/18) \u2014 positive but weakly evidenced; the form's evidence mass sits in folds 1/2/3/5. RECLASSIFIED AS INVALID: nooi-union T2.5/T5 (fold4 negative), v1-union T1.25 (LOFO-min +7.6 = 25% retained -> fold2-concentrated) and T2.5 (neg fold + concentration), xproto T0.625/T1.25 (LOFO-min ~25% retained -> concentrated) and T2.5 (2 neg folds), v1 mean-rank ens t5 +12.99 (fold5 -2.0), v2 ens t5 (neg fold + BOOT floor -3.91), nooi ens t1 (fold1 neg). METHOD NOTE: the earlier 'fold2 carries the sum' reads used sum-% (n x EV) which conflates trade DENSITY with per-trade edge; per-trade per-fold EV is the gate-relevant quantity, and under it the nooi-union T1.25 edge exists year-round with burst folds contributing extra TRADES at higher EV (legitimate) rather than being the only profitable period. Pending: rev7 8-seed pools + the 16-member xproto-nooi union will be evaluated under this gate directly.", "note": "Full audit log gate_audit.log; union jsons now carry perfold_ev/perfold_n/lofo/gate fields."}
